window.ADORN_SEARCH=[{"title":"Adorn & ASF wiki","group":"Start here","section":"","path":"index.html","text":"This wiki covers Adorn and Adorn Seller Framework (ASF): what each mod does, how to use it, and how to create and share your own content. The contents on the left organise the guides by mod and purpose. The list on the right follows the headings of the page you are reading."},{"title":"Adorn & ASF wiki","group":"Start here","section":"Adorn","path":"index.html#adorn","text":"## Adorn Adorn is an in-game outfit studio for your character, NPCs and factions. Browse the clothing and armour supplied by your installed mods, combine pieces into custom looks and inspect them in a rotatable 3D preview. Give a follower their own style, coordinate a group, keep a personal wardrobe and share assignment contributions with other players. You can start with an installed set, replace a few pieces or assemble a look from several mods. Compare a recipient’s current outfit with your proposal, save the assignment and return to it later to edit, disable or remove it. Personal saved looks stay with the loaded save; NPC and faction rules are shared configuration."},{"title":"Adorn & ASF wiki","group":"Start here","section":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","path":"index.html#adorn-seller-framework-asf","text":"## Adorn Seller Framework (ASF) Adorn Seller Framework (ASF) connects those looks to a seller, a challenge and a reward. Find the assigned character, solve their request and earn finished pieces or learn to craft your selection—even supported pieces whose original mod has no recipe. Its in-game author tools let creators configure the seller, write and record the conversation, build native dialogue, and choose the crafting and riddle rules. A tailor, a demanding collector, or a follower with an unusual side business. For players, ASF makes acquiring a chosen look part of play. For NPC authors and modlist creators, it provides a way to build a service around a character: their exchanges, the performance behind each reply, the requests they make and the crafting rules attached to their rewards. Prepared conversations can combine stock Skyrim recordings, personal takes and silent replies."},{"title":"Adorn & ASF wiki","group":"Start here","section":"Author tools","path":"index.html#author-tools","text":"## Author tools Create the content used by ASF: recipe instructions and materials, item-payment riddles, optional hints and prepared seller replies. The author guides explain how these parts fit together before taking you through each editor. Recipes define the separate cost of crafting each reward piece. Riddles define the seller’s item payment, with optional reward tiers and an extra clue. Authors can write manually or request optional OpenRouter suggestions, review the result and decide what to save. The dialogue builder prepares matching native records and audio for the next launch."},{"title":"Adorn & ASF wiki","group":"Start here","section":"Reference","path":"index.html#reference","text":"## Reference Find the supporting details for configuration, saves, backups, file formats and implementation limits. Use the reference alongside the task guides when maintaining or sharing a setup. This section explains which data belongs to a save, how configuration priority works and which prepared files must remain together when backing up an installation or sharing authored content."},{"title":"Adorn & ASF wiki","group":"Start here","section":"Before you begin","path":"index.html#before-you-begin","text":"## Before you begin Check the requirements for your role. Ordinary players using prepared ASF content do not need the dialogue-build toolchain or an API key. The compatibility and limits guide explains the content requirements and capacity limits that affect your setup."},{"title":"Installation requirements","group":"Start here","section":"","path":"start/requirements.html","text":"Adorn and Adorn Seller Framework (ASF) have different installation needs, and creating new seller dialogue requires tools that ordinary players do not need. Use this page to identify the requirements for your role before following either mod’s setup guide. Adorn is the standalone outfit mod; Adorn Seller Framework (ASF) is its optional companion. Install the runtime requirements for the mods you use. Only authors building changed dialogue/audio need the additional author tools below."},{"title":"Installation requirements","group":"Start here","section":"Supported setup","path":"start/requirements.html#supported-setup","text":"## Supported setup Adorn and Adorn Seller Framework (ASF) have only been tested within an MO2 modlist on Windows. Other mod managers and standalone installations are untested. Use Mod Organizer 2 (MO2) for the documented installation and authoring workflows. Install versions of SKSE and every native dependency that match your Skyrim executable. Support for another runtime in an individual dependency does not establish compatibility for the complete Adorn/ASF setup."},{"title":"Installation requirements","group":"Start here","section":"Runtime requirements for Adorn","path":"start/requirements.html#runtime-requirements-for-adorn","text":"## Runtime requirements for Adorn | Requirement | Official download or project page | Purpose | | --- | --- | --- | | SKSE64 | SKSE / Nexus | Native plugin loading; match the installed Skyrim executable | | Address Library for SKSE Plugins | Nexus | Native address resolution; match the game build | | Prisma UI | Nexus | Adorn's in-game interface; follow Prisma's own requirements | | SkyUI | Nexus | MCM interface | | MCM Helper | Nexus | MCM settings, hotkeys and persistence | | SkyPatcher | Nexus | Generated NPC/faction assignment rules on launch | Prisma UI currently lists Media Keys Fix SKSE or Keyboard Shortcuts Fix, plus Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable 2022 x64. Follow the linked Prisma page for the current alternatives and downloads. The core archive requires AdornSlots.esp to be enabled, alongside its native DLL, matching UI/scripts and helper assets. Enabling only the ESP is not a complete installation. ### BodySlide, bodies and outfit assets BodySlide and Outfit Studio is strongly recommended for Adorn's full outfit-browsing experience. BodySlide projects, groups and built outfit meshes are a major part of Adorn's browsing workflow. Install the original clothing mods and their required body setup. For outfits that require BodySlide output, build those outfits in BodySlide before using them in Adorn, and enable the output in MO2. Adorn detects and previews installed meshes; Refresh builds rescans them rather than running BodySlide or creating missing meshes. Plugin-outfit browsing can also use existing installed meshes without BodySlide projects. This does not remove the body or build requirements of the clothing itself. Adorn does not convert outfits between bodies or fix clipping. BHUNP compatibility has not been verified; do not assume a BodySlide project alone establishes support."},{"title":"Installation requirements","group":"Start here","section":"Additional runtime requirements for ASF","path":"start/requirements.html#additional-runtime-requirements-for-asf","text":"## Additional runtime requirements for ASF | Requirement | Purpose | | --- | --- | | Adorn | ASF uses Adorn's DLL, UI, content and progression systems. Requires the complete Adorn installation | | Fuz Ro D-oh – Silent Voice | Runtime-specific download for readable unvoiced fallback replies; required for the current fallback paths | | Pack-specific NPC/content mods | Only when the chosen authored seller pack references them; the generic framework has no universal follower requirement | Enable Adorn Seller Framework.esp as well as AdornSlots.esp. The current generic framework is NPC-neutral and starts disabled/unassigned. One placed seller is active at a time; prepared drafts may cover multiple NPCs. Keep Fuz Ro D-oh installed for the supported unvoiced fallback replies, including when your authored pack contains prepared silent audio. Ordinary players using prepared content need no API key, Python, Creation Kit, BSArch or development SDK."},{"title":"Installation requirements","group":"Start here","section":"Authoring tools","path":"start/requirements.html#authoring-tools","text":"## Authoring tools Players using prepared seller content do not need to install this authoring toolchain. It is for authors building new or changed dialogue/audio, including prepared extra-clue replies. Manual riddle/recipe text editing alone does not require the audio tools. ### Included with ASF — no separate installation The complete ASF author bundle already supplies the following tools. You do not need to download or install additional copies for the normal Build workflow. | Included tool | What it does | Installation | | --- | --- | --- | | ASF dialogue builder | Builds the native dialogue records and supporting output using self-contained SellerDialogueBuild.exe | Bundled with ASF; no separate .NET SDK needed | | Portable eSpeak NG 1.52.0 | Supplies temporary timing guides for silent replies, with its data/notices/matching source; its audible speech is not packaged | Bundled with ASF; no separate eSpeak installation needed | | FFmpeg | Normalizes imported and recorded audio using the supplied Windows x64 build | Bundled with ASF; no separate FFmpeg installation needed | ### Install separately — only for dialogue/audio authoring | Tool | What you need to do | | --- | --- | | Python 3 | Not bundled. Install separately for the voice preparation/staging scripts. | | Skyrim Special Edition Creation Kit | Not bundled with ASF. Install the Creation Kit from Steam. It supplies LipGenerator, xwmaencode and LIPFuzer; these are Creation Kit tools, not three additional ASF downloads. | The build expects the CK tools in their installed CK/game locations: Tools/LipGen/LipGenerator/LipGenerator.exe, Tools/Audio/xwmaencode.exe and Tools/LipGen/LipFuzer/LIPFuzer.exe. Bundled FFmpeg and eSpeak do not replace them. ### BSArch requirement for stock Skyrim voice replies BSArch is an authoring requirement when building seller dialogue that uses stock Skyrim recordings. It is not bundled with ASF. It extracts the installed game's voice archive into a local cache; a fresh stock-voice setup needs it even if another author's existing cache did not. BSArch is included with xEdit builds, as confirmed by its author. Check your existing xEdit/SSEEdit folder for BSArch.exe first: if it is already at the path below, no extra download is needed. ASF uses this command-line tool, not the xEdit editor. BSArch is separate from the Creation Kit; installing CK does not supply the executable ASF calls. 1. Check your xEdit/SSEEdit installation for BSArch.exe. If missing, download the BSArch command-line tool from the author's Nexus Files page, rather than the separate BSArchPro GUI. The standalone tool's page is hosted under Fallout New Vegas; ASF uses it to extract Skyrim's voice archive. 2. Extract it into tools\\xEdit inside the MO2 instance used for Adorn. Create those folders if needed and keep the downloaded package's accompanying files together. 3. Confirm the executable is directly at \\tools\\xEdit\\BSArch.exe, with no extra nested download folder. For example, an instance at N:\\NSW needs N:\\NSW\\tools\\xEdit\\BSArch.exe. 4. Keep the game's Data\\Skyrim - Voices_en0.bsa available. The current stock-recording workflow expects that English voice archive. The current publisher looks at that exact MO2-relative path. Do not install BSArch as a normal mod in the left pane; no MO2 executable entry is needed. ASF invokes it automatically when preparing stock recordings. CK's Archive.exe is not a configured replacement. Players using a prepared seller pack do not need BSArch. Authors using only silent or their own imported/recorded replies do not need stock extraction. Once an extraction cache exists, ASF reuses it while the voice archive is unchanged; keep BSArch installed for future rebuilds. BSArch source code in the xEdit repository. ### Optional writing assistance | Tool or service | When needed | Bundled? | | --- | --- | --- | | OpenRouter account/key | Optional writing suggestions using the author's chosen model/credit. No requirement for manual writing, gameplay or dialogue builds. | Not included or required; use your own account/key only if you enable assistance. | Build [seller]'s seller dialogue saves drafts and prepares the output while Skyrim runs. After Build complete, save and exit; the publisher installs after Skyrim exits, into the resolved Configs/Overwrite destination. Wait for installation then restart. Prepare clue dialogue uses the same pipeline. See ASF guide and User data."},{"title":"Compatibility & limits","group":"Start here","section":"","path":"start/release-status.html","text":"Adorn and Adorn Seller Framework (ASF) use the outfits, NPCs and supporting tools installed in your game. This page explains the practical limits to consider when choosing content, configuring assignments or preparing a seller setup."},{"title":"Compatibility & limits","group":"Start here","section":"Installation compatibility","path":"start/release-status.html#installation-compatibility","text":"## Installation compatibility Both Adorn and Adorn Seller Framework have only been tested within an MO2 modlist on Windows. These guides use that setup; other mod managers and standalone installations are untested. Check the runtime information supplied with your mod download and install versions of SKSE and native dependencies that match your Skyrim executable. A dependency supporting another runtime does not automatically make the complete Adorn installation compatible with it. The original clothing and NPC mods remain required. Assignment packs and seller configuration reference their records; they do not supply those mods’ meshes, textures or characters."},{"title":"Compatibility & limits","group":"Start here","section":"Outfits and preview","path":"start/release-status.html#outfits-and-preview","text":"## Outfits and preview A custom look supports up to 32 pieces. The selected pieces must have compatible equipment slots, meshes and body variants. Combining them does not resolve clipping, create missing male/female meshes or convert clothing between bodies. BodySlide is strongly recommended for the full browsing workflow. Adorn displays the installed meshes; build the output required by your clothing and enable it in MO2 first. Refreshing Adorn’s builds rescans that output rather than running BodySlide. BHUNP compatibility has not been verified."},{"title":"Compatibility & limits","group":"Start here","section":"Assignments and sharing","path":"start/release-status.html#assignments-and-sharing","text":"## Assignments and sharing Custom NPC/faction assignments share 64 outfit slots. Disabled custom rules still reserve their slots. Installed plugin outfits do not use that custom bank, and an imported source group can share a slot across its accepted recipients. NPC assignments target the NPC base record, so copies of the same base can share the result. Faction assignments exclude child races. Direct child contributions require compatible clothing, local preview and explicit approval. Version 1 assignment packs support up to 512 groups, 4,096 recipients and 8 MB. Missing defining plugins or changed record identities can prevent a contribution from resolving."},{"title":"Compatibility & limits","group":"Start here","section":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","path":"start/release-status.html#adorn-seller-framework-asf","text":"## Adorn Seller Framework (ASF) One placed NPC holds the active seller role at a time. Authors can retain conversation drafts for several NPCs, but choosing another draft does not create a second simultaneous seller service. Learned recipe orders share 32 craftable-piece slots per save. An order with several pieces uses capacity for those pieces. Finished-outfit orders use no recipe slots. The tiered offer journal holds up to 512 distinct offers in that save. Changed seller dialogue requires Build → exit Skyrim → installation → restart. Saving a draft or choosing a recording alone does not activate new native dialogue."},{"title":"Compatibility & limits","group":"Start here","section":"Optional writing assistance","path":"start/release-status.html#optional-writing-assistance","text":"## Optional writing assistance OpenRouter assistance requires your own account/key and a compatible available model route. Free capacity and provider restrictions can vary. If a request fails, the editor keeps your manual work; review the error before retrying. ASF does not silently substitute a paid model. Manual writing and normal gameplay do not require an API key or internet connection. Tier rules start disabled, and the starter riddle pool is example content for authors to expand and balance."},{"title":"Compatibility & limits","group":"Start here","section":"Asking for help","path":"start/release-status.html#asking-for-help","text":"## Asking for help Include your game and mod versions, input device, selected pieces or seller, the steps taken and the expected versus actual result. Keep relevant logs and leave API keys out of reports. Use Adorn troubleshooting for outfit, preview and assignment problems, or ASF troubleshooting for orders, recordings and dialogue builds."},{"title":"Introduction to Adorn","group":"Adorn","section":"","path":"adorn/introduction.html","text":"Adorn is an in-game outfit studio for your character, NPCs and factions. It brings the clothing and armour in your installed mods into one place to browse, combine, preview and assign. You can give a favourite follower a signature look, coordinate a faction, or build a personal wardrobe without leaving Skyrim to manage each outfit change. Adorn works with the items and meshes your modlist already supplies. The creative choices are yours: start with a complete installed set, replace a few pieces, or assemble a new combination from several mods."},{"title":"Introduction to Adorn","group":"Adorn","section":"Explore your collection","path":"adorn/introduction.html#explore-your-collection","text":"## Explore your collection Browse installed plugin outfits, search individual pieces by name, EditorID or source plugin, and explore detected BodySlide groups where supported. A complete set can be a useful starting point; an individual piece can finish a look you already have in mind. Custom looks support up to 32 pieces. Add a full set, remove what you do not want, and mix compatible clothing, armour and accessories. Source labels and build warnings help you understand what is available and which meshes are being used."},{"title":"Introduction to Adorn","group":"Adorn","section":"See what you are choosing","path":"adorn/introduction.html#see-what-you-are-choosing","text":"## See what you are choosing The rotatable 3D preview uses your installed outfit meshes. Inspect a combination as you build it and select the preview body sex. For a selected recipient, Their outfit / Your outfit lets you compare their current look with the one you are preparing. Previewing is part of the design process; saving an assignment is the step that applies your decision. Mesh compatibility, equipment slots and clipping still depend on the pieces you choose. Adorn does not build missing BodySlide meshes or convert clothing between bodies."},{"title":"Introduction to Adorn","group":"Adorn","section":"Dress characters and groups","path":"adorn/introduction.html#dress-characters-and-groups","text":"## Dress characters and groups Find a recipient through nearby actors, the crosshair or the active-modlist search. Assign a look to an NPC, a faction, or a named group containing several recipients. Faction rules can keep individual exclusions, while direct NPC assignments take priority over faction assignments. That lets you give a group a common identity and still keep a particular character's own style. NPC assignments target the character's base record, so copies made from that base can share the result. The Assignments view keeps those decisions together. Search, edit, disable or remove a rule as your plans change. Saved assignments can dress eligible nearby actors and generate SkyPatcher rules for the next launch."},{"title":"Introduction to Adorn","group":"Adorn","section":"Keep a personal wardrobe","path":"adorn/introduction.html#keep-a-personal-wardrobe","text":"## Keep a personal wardrobe Save and name favourite looks under Assign → Player, then open the compact Quick saved outfits picker through its MCM binding. Your character can have travelling clothes, everyday wear and a collection of outfits worth returning to. The personal wardrobe belongs to the loaded save. NPC and faction assignments are shared configuration used by saves loading those files. The saves and backups guide explains what to preserve when moving or updating your installation."},{"title":"Introduction to Adorn","group":"Adorn","section":"Share your choices","path":"adorn/introduction.html#share-your-choices","text":"## Share your choices Assignment sharing exports contributions for other players to review. Imports show recipients, dependencies and conflicts before applying accepted changes; attribution travels with the contribution. Packs carry assignments and item references. The original clothing and NPC mods supply their own assets and remain required. See assignment sharing for the review and merge workflow."},{"title":"Introduction to Adorn","group":"Adorn","section":"How Adorn and ASF fit together","path":"adorn/introduction.html#how-adorn-and-asf-fit-together","text":"## How Adorn and ASF fit together Adorn works on its own for outfit browsing, assignments and the ordinary player wardrobe. Adorn Seller Framework (ASF) is an optional companion mod that connects selected looks to a seller, an item-payment challenge and either finished-piece or learnable-recipe rewards. If you want to dress the world, begin with Adorn. If you also want your character to earn their chosen looks through a seller service, read the introduction to ASF. The compatibility and limits guide explains the assignment bank, content compatibility and other practical limits."},{"title":"Getting started","group":"Adorn","section":"","path":"adorn/getting-started.html","text":"This guide takes you from installing Adorn to opening its outfit studio and making your first selection. Start here if you are new to the mod; the setup steps and worked example explain how browsing, previewing and saving fit together."},{"title":"Getting started","group":"Adorn","section":"Requirements","path":"adorn/getting-started.html#requirements","text":"## Requirements | Component | Purpose | | --- | --- | | SKSE64 | Native plugin loading; use the build matching your Skyrim executable | | Address Library | Native address resolution | | Prisma UI | In-game interface | | SkyUI | MCM | | MCM Helper | Persistent settings and key bindings | | SkyPatcher | Assignment rules on launch | Follow Prisma UI's own requirements, currently including Media Keys Fix SKSE or Keyboard Shortcuts Fix, and Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable 2022 x64. BodySlide is strongly recommended. Adorn's BodySlide browsing uses your installed projects, groups and built meshes. Install BodySlide and Outfit Studio, the original clothing mods and their required body setup. Build outfits that require BodySlide, then enable the output in MO2 before browsing. Adorn's Refresh builds detects existing output; it does not build meshes. Plugin outfits with ready-made meshes can also be browsed without BodySlide projects. BHUNP compatibility has not been verified. Tested installation: Windows with MO2. Both Adorn and ASF have only been tested inside an MO2 modlist; other managers and standalone installs are untested. The full requirements distinguish player dependencies from author tools. ASF is an optional module with its own additional requirements. It is not needed for standalone assignments or the ordinary player wardrobe."},{"title":"Getting started","group":"Adorn","section":"Install and open","path":"adorn/getting-started.html#install-and-open","text":"## Install and open 1. Install the runtime requirements. Use builds matching your Skyrim executable. 2. Install and enable Adorn in MO2. Enable AdornSlots.esp in the Plugins pane. 3. If supplied, enable Adorn Configs below Adorn in the left pane. That folder holds editable configuration separately from runtime updates. 4. Launch SKSE through MO2, load your save and press F6. Change the key in MCM → Adorn → Open / close Adorn if needed. Launch through MO2 so Adorn can see your enabled clothing, configuration and BodySlide output. Match all native dependencies to your installed Skyrim executable."},{"title":"Getting started","group":"Adorn","section":"Worked example","path":"adorn/getting-started.html#worked-example","text":"## Worked example To dress a faction while preserving one member's look: 1. Choose a modest installed outfit and inspect it. 2. Open Assign → Factions, select the intended faction and inspect members. 3. Exclude the member whose clothes should remain. Add the faction to Selected recipients and save. 4. Check several nearby members, then verify again after restarting Skyrim. 5. Choose another look and make a direct assignment for a different member. That actor should use the direct rule while other eligible members use the faction look. 6. Change the faction outfit through Assignments and confirm the exclusion/direct override remain effective. 7. Export the rules through Share assignments and inspect their dependencies/conflicts in import review. 8. Remove the test rules through Assignments, follow retirement feedback, restart and verify the intended restoration. Use a separate test configuration if the shared change should not affect other characters. A test save alone does not isolate assignment files."},{"title":"Outfits & preview","group":"Adorn","section":"","path":"adorn/outfits-and-preview.html","text":"An outfit in Adorn can be a complete installed set or a custom combination of pieces from your collection. This guide explains how to find those pieces, understand their sources and use the preview before applying the result."},{"title":"Outfits & preview","group":"Adorn","section":"Choose an outfit","path":"adorn/outfits-and-preview.html#choose-an-outfit","text":"## Choose an outfit Start in Outfits. Installed outfit → Browse outfits searches the active modlist. Choose a result, inspect its pieces and preview, then select Use this outfit where offered. Switch to Custom outfit to choose individual pieces. You can also add an installed set to the custom look and edit it. A custom look supports up to 32 pieces. Armour and clothing still need compatible body slots and meshes; combining them does not resolve clipping or two items using the same slot. Where available, BodySlide and Plugin outfits select the browsing source. BodySlide groups help find built content. If the wrong build folder is detected, use Output folder → Scan this folder and choose the folder containing the built meshes. Refresh builds rescans; Adorn does not run BodySlide or build missing meshes. ### Build a custom look step by step 1. Choose Custom outfit → Add armor piece. 2. Search by name, EditorID or source plugin. Check the intended variant and equipment slots. 3. Add compatible pieces, or start from an installed set with Add full set to custom outfit. 4. Review each row in the custom-piece list beside the preview. Remove unwanted pieces through that row's remove action. 5. When selecting replacements for a BodySlide look's occupied slots, inspect the resulting kept/replaced pieces before saving. 6. Name the look where offered, choose recipients or Player, then use the appropriate Save action. A custom look combines item records. It does not create new mesh assets, convert bodies, alter enchantments or resolve incompatible slot definitions. ### Understand BodySlide source warnings A detected project/output is not proof that its mesh wins every conflict. Pay attention to overridden/ambiguous warnings: another mod can replace output, and several projects can produce the same file. Adorn's preview uses the current winning game meshes. Male/Female filters narrow availability; they do not create missing variants. The originating plugin and the mod currently winning the meshes may differ. Check the output folder and source labels before rebuilding anything."},{"title":"Outfits & preview","group":"Adorn","section":"Read the preview","path":"adorn/outfits-and-preview.html#read-the-preview","text":"## Read the preview Drag the model or use its right-stick control to rotate. Auto, Female and Male select preview body sex. When inspecting an NPC or faction member, Their outfit / Your outfit compares the existing and proposed look. A preview is not an equip action. Meshes and textures come from the active installation. A blank body part, wrong shape or clipping should first be checked against the clothing's body requirements, available meshes and your BodySlide build. The preview is not a guarantee that every race, child body or physics combination will render identically on an actor in game. Use + / − in the header to change text size. The four colour dots choose the interface palette. Pause game and Play control the interface's play/pause flow; follow the visible focus state when returning to gameplay."},{"title":"Outfits & preview","group":"Adorn","section":"Optional preview extras","path":"adorn/outfits-and-preview.html#optional-preview-extras","text":"## Optional preview extras The current build includes a TNG male-preview reveal behind the 200% text-size joke and Show more / Hide more. It requires relevant installed anatomy assets and is confined to the supported adult male static preview. It does not dress/equip an actor. Female, child and quick previews have no such switch."},{"title":"NPCs, factions & groups","group":"Adorn","section":"","path":"adorn/assignments.html","text":"Assignments decide which look an NPC or faction should wear. This guide covers choosing recipients, combining them into groups, preserving individual exceptions and managing the saved rules as your choices change."},{"title":"NPCs, factions & groups","group":"Adorn","section":"Assign to one NPC","path":"adorn/assignments.html#assign-to-one-npc","text":"## Assign to one NPC 1. Choose the outfit first. 2. Open Assign → NPCs. Use Nearby now, search the active modlist, or use the crosshair NPC where offered. 3. Add the intended recipient and review Selected recipients. Clear unintended recipients before saving. 4. Inspect the preview and select Save assignment. 5. Open Assignments to find the saved rule. Check the actor now and after a complete Skyrim restart. An NPC assignment targets the base NPC, even when selected through a nearby reference. Other copies of that base can receive the same outfit. It is not a rule limited to the one actor standing in front of you. Location information is available when Adorn can resolve a loaded or previously observed actor. Last seen in is session information, not continuous tracking. Teleport to appears only when an available reference is unambiguous; it moves the player to that reference and does not create an NPC."},{"title":"NPCs, factions & groups","group":"Adorn","section":"Assign to a faction or group","path":"adorn/assignments.html#assign-to-a-faction-or-group","text":"## Assign to a faction or group In Assign → Factions, choose the faction, inspect its members and exclude those who should keep their own clothes. Add the faction to Selected recipients. NPC and faction recipients can share one named group and look. Save when the entire recipient list is correct. A direct NPC assignment takes priority over its faction assignment. If a member keeps a different Adorn outfit, check for an existing direct rule before changing the faction. Faction rules exclude child races. A direct child assignment needs compatible child meshes, local preview and explicit approval; approval from someone else's shared pack does not carry over. The native custom bank has 64 slots. A custom recipient group shares one slot; disabled custom rules still reserve slots. Installed plugin outfits use none of that custom bank. Free capacity by removing unused custom rules through Adorn, then follow any retirement/restart instructions shown."},{"title":"NPCs, factions & groups","group":"Adorn","section":"Edit or remove assignments","path":"adorn/assignments.html#edit-or-remove-assignments","text":"## Edit or remove assignments Use Assignments to select, edit, disable or delete saved rules. Saving updates eligible nearby actors and writes the next-launch SkyPatcher rules. Restart Skyrim to verify the persistent result for actors outside the current area. Keep Adorn installed while removing rules you no longer want. Generated patches and actor changes can outlive disabling a runtime folder. Another outfit manager or actor script can also reapply clothing. Do not use deletion of rules.json or all of Overwrite as routine troubleshooting. Assignments are installation configuration. All saves using those files see them. A new character does not reset NPC/faction assignments, and a separate MO2 profile may still use the same physical Configs or Overwrite files."},{"title":"Your wardrobe","group":"Adorn","section":"","path":"adorn/wardrobe.html","text":"The player wardrobe keeps named looks for the character in your loaded save. Use it to organise favourite outfits and switch between them through Adorn or its compact picker; ownership rules depend on whether ordinary Adorn or ASF seller mode is active."},{"title":"Your wardrobe","group":"Adorn","section":"Use the player wardrobe","path":"adorn/wardrobe.html#use-the-player-wardrobe","text":"## Use the player wardrobe Choose the look, then open Assign → Player. Name it and select Save outfit. The saved list belongs to the loaded save; save the game before exiting. Back up the matching .ess and .skse files together. | Mode | Item and wear behavior | | --- | --- | | Ordinary standalone play | Give items supplies chosen pieces. Wear now and saved Wear supply missing base pieces before equipping. | | Developer tools unlocked | Give is hidden/rejected; Wear requires already owned pieces. This mode is intended for authoring. | | Seller mode active | Direct Give and unsaved Wear are blocked; saved Wear requires ownership. Obtain new pieces through the seller/crafting loop. | To use the compact picker, bind MCM → Adorn → Quick saved outfits to a key different from the main opening key. It starts unbound. The picker uses this save's saved looks and the same ownership rules. If upgrading from the old shared wardrobe file, Recover old saved outfits… explicitly copies those looks into the current save. Use it only on the intended character. It leaves the old file intact and grants no items; new games do not import it automatically."},{"title":"Controls & interface","group":"Adorn","section":"","path":"adorn/controls.html","text":"Adorn supports mouse, keyboard and controller navigation, with MCM bindings for its main window and quick wardrobe. This page identifies the controls and explains which views handle outfit design, recipients, saved assignments and author tools."},{"title":"Controls & interface","group":"Adorn","section":"Controls","path":"adorn/controls.html#controls","text":"## Controls Mouse users can scroll the pane under the pointer. Controller users move focus with the left stick/D-pad and use the displayed Accept/Back actions. Shoulder buttons move between panes where available; right-stick behavior depends on the current view, rotating the outfit preview or scrolling an authoring pane. In Riddles, right-stick up/down scrolls the focused pane. If text or settings extend below a pane, scroll that pane rather than the whole workspace."},{"title":"Controls & interface","group":"Adorn","section":"Interface reference","path":"adorn/controls.html#interface-reference","text":"## Interface reference | View/control | Responsibility | | --- | --- | | Outfits | Browse installed looks and assemble custom pieces | | Assign → NPCs | Nearby actors, active-modlist search and NPC selection | | Assign → Factions | Faction/member browsing and exclusions | | Assign → Player | Save/wear personal looks and use optional seller orders | | Selected recipients | Review the entire NPC/faction group before saving | | Assignments | Existing rules, edit/disable/delete and contribution sharing | | Their outfit / Your outfit | Compare the recipient's existing look with your draft | | Auto / Female / Male | Preview body sex | | Header + / − | Text scale | | Preview colour dots | Pine, sky, grey or pink | | Play / Pause game | Interface play/pause control | | X or opening key | Close/toggle Adorn | | Quick saved outfits | Compact player wardrobe, with a separately bound MCM key | | Seller / Riddles / Recipes | Author tools, documented in the ASF manual | Previewing prepares a choice. Save assignment, Save outfit, Give items and Wear now have different effects. Read the action/status before assuming an actor or saved rule has changed."},{"title":"Share assignments","group":"Adorn","section":"","path":"adorn/sharing.html","text":"Adorn exports and imports NPC/faction assignment packs from inside the game. Export pack opens Save As so you choose a location; Import pack opens a file chooser so you can select a downloaded JSON anywhere. The chosen import opens for review before any assignments change. Folder copying and a game restart are not required for either action. Recipients merge accepted targets into their own rules.json. Imports use the existing assignment save, retirement, live dressing, child policy, and generated SkyPatcher paths. Installing a contribution never applies it automatically."},{"title":"Share assignments","group":"Adorn","section":"Contribute","path":"adorn/sharing.html#contribute","text":"## Contribute 1. Dress NPCs or factions through Assign as usual. 2. Open Assignments → Share assignments and enter a pack name, contributor name, and optional description. 3. Tick Include in export beside the assignments to share, or choose Select all assignments. Select all includes assignments outside the current search. 4. Choose Export pack, choose a filename and location in Save As, and save. Share that JSON. Windows asks before replacing an existing file. The export goes to the location you chose, such as Downloads or Desktop. Exporting changes neither saved assignments nor generated SkyPatcher files. Cancelling Save As saves no file. Export refuses the active SKSE settings locations to avoid accidentally replacing working configuration; the optional AssignmentPacks folder remains an allowed destination."},{"title":"Share assignments","group":"Adorn","section":"Review and merge","path":"adorn/sharing.html#review-and-merge","text":"## Review and merge 1. Open Assignments → Share assignments → Import pack while Skyrim is running. 2. Select the downloaded/exported JSON in the Windows Open dialog. Adorn opens its review screen directly; the original file does not need to be copied into a mod folder. Cancelling file selection imports nothing and preserves an existing review. 3. Review the outfit, pieces, recipient, enabled state, required plugins, faction exclusions, and custom-slot capacity. Each row is one recipient, so part of a mixed group can be accepted while the rest stays unchanged. 4. New recipients default to Add contribution. Overlapping direct assignments default to Keep existing; explicitly choose Use contribution to replace them. Identical assignments are skipped. Missing records or incompatible record types block the affected recipients. 5. Choose Import selected contributions. Adorn rechecks the current assignments and dependencies, stages all selected groups, allocates local IDs and outfit slots, captures this installation's original outfits, and saves the batch through its existing commit path. Validation, capacity, or baseline-capture failure before commit leaves the saved files unchanged. The existing commit path attempts rollback if a file write fails. Accepted contributions become ordinary assignments in rules.json; removing the source JSON does not uninstall them. Edit, disable, or delete them through Assignments. A review becomes invalid when working assignments change; review again before importing. Contributor credit is shown on imported rows and preserved by edits and re-export. Nearby matching NPCs can dress after import. A full Skyrim restart is a separate check that the generated SkyPatcher rules apply on launch. ### Optional installed-pack library Modlist authors can still supply JSON at SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/AssignmentPacks/ in an enabled MO2 mod, Adorn Configs, or Overwrite. Expand Installed packs (optional), refresh, select a file, and review it. The Exports subfolder is excluded from automatic discovery, but Import pack can open a file there directly. This library is optional; normal sharing uses the Open and Save dialogs."},{"title":"Share assignments","group":"Adorn","section":"Preserved behavior and limits","path":"adorn/sharing.html#preserved-behavior-and-limits","text":"## Preserved behavior and limits - Installed outfits and custom looks of up to 32 pieces are shareable. NPC/faction groups, group names, enabled states, preview/body sex choices, source labels, and faction exclusions travel with them. Disabled contributions stay disabled. - Direct NPC assignments retain priority over factions. Accepting a faction does not erase separate direct NPC choices. Replacing one recipient in a group retains the other recipients. An explicitly empty incoming faction exclusion list replaces prior exclusions when that faction's contribution is accepted. - Faction outfits retain the existing exclusion of child races. Direct child outfits can be exported but are blocked in import review: preview and explicitly approve a compatible outfit locally through Assign. Contributor approval is never treated as local approval. - Saved player outfits, seller assignments, dialogue, recordings, recipes, and riddles keep their separate stores and are outside an assignment pack. No game saves, generated INIs, local rule IDs, slot numbers, runtime FormIDs, restoration history, or original-outfit snapshots are exported. - Plugin names and local FormIDs identify records. Compatible defining plugins and records must exist in the active order; compaction, renaming, or changed FormIDs can require reassignment. Mods, meshes, and textures are not bundled. - The bank remains 64 custom outfit slots. One accepted source group shares one slot across accepted recipients. Disabled custom rules reserve slots too. Imported groups need free slots as they are staged; a full bank can reject a custom replacement until space is freed. Installed outfits use no custom slots. Sharing changes no slot-bank ESP or plugin records. - Version 1 supports up to 512 assignment groups, 4096 total recipients, and 8 MB per file. Split larger contributions into multiple packs."},{"title":"Share assignments","group":"Adorn","section":"Format and implementation","path":"adorn/sharing.html#format-and-implementation","text":"## Format and implementation Version 1 contains format: \"AdornAssignmentPack\", version: 1, name, author, description, derived requiredPlugins, and assignments. Each assignment carries targets, outfit, and optional carried-forward contributor credit. Portable normalization discards unknown fields and derives dependencies from the records themselves. Duplicate recipients in one pack are rejected as ambiguous. src/AssignmentPack.cpp owns normalization, export, conflict review, and selection. src/RuleStage.cpp contains the existing validation, slot allocation, recipient replacement, and retirement algorithm shared by ordinary Save and batch import. src/RuleStore.cpp owns discovery, immutable review snapshots, and the single commit. src/PackFileDialog.cpp runs the Windows Open/Save chooser on its own STA worker; PackTransfer.cpp handles bounded reads, UTF-8 path reporting, and completed-file replacement. Selected export content is captured before Save As opens. Review and game-state work return through Skyrim's task interface; live dressing happens only after successful commit. The native dialog follows Microsoft's Common Item Dialog API."},{"title":"Share assignments","group":"Adorn","section":"Troubleshooting","path":"adorn/sharing.html#troubleshooting","text":"## Troubleshooting If a contribution is blocked, check its defining plugins and review the displayed reason before importing. Custom groups need free assignment slots, including while replacements are staged. If an accepted outfit does not appear, check that its assignment is enabled and the required clothing mods are loaded. Generated SkyPatcher rules apply on the next Skyrim launch. When reporting an issue, include the affected recipients, your merge choices and the relevant AdornLive.log and SkyPatcher.log entries."},{"title":"Troubleshooting Adorn","group":"Adorn","section":"","path":"adorn/troubleshooting.html","text":"Use this guide when Adorn’s outfits, preview, assignments or wardrobe behave differently from what you expect. It brings common checks, update and backup guidance, and capacity limits together so you can narrow down the problem and prepare a useful report."},{"title":"Troubleshooting Adorn","group":"Adorn","section":"Troubleshooting","path":"adorn/troubleshooting.html#troubleshooting","text":"## Troubleshooting | Symptom | Check and next action | | --- | --- | | F6 does nothing | Check the MCM binding, launch through SKSE, confirm AdornSlots.esp is enabled and Prisma UI plus its input/runtime requirements load. Read AdornLive.log and skse64.log. | | MCM or author tabs missing | Check SkyUI/MCM Helper and matched scripts/config. Seller/Riddles/Recipes are author tools; ordinary use needs no author unlock. | | Outfit does not appear in browsing | Confirm its defining plugin is active. Search by name, EditorID or source; for BodySlide content refresh and check Output folder. | | Preview incomplete or wrong body | Check installed clothing/body meshes and actual BodySlide output. Include the selected body sex, pieces and source mod in a report. | | Clothes change back | Check direct-versus-faction rules, another outfit manager/follower script and later SkyPatcher rules. Verify generated-file priority and retest after a full restart. | | Custom bank full | Disabled custom assignments still reserve slots. Remove unused rules and follow retirement feedback, or use an installed outfit. | | Wardrobe appears on the wrong character or disappears | Confirm the intended save and matching co-save. New wardrobes are save-specific; use explicit legacy recovery only on the intended character. | | Starter config appears ignored | Check Overwrite for personal files that correctly take precedence. Back them up before any move; do not clear unrelated Overwrite content. | | Import blocked | Read the affected row's dependency, record-type or capacity explanation. Review again if assignments changed while the review was open. | For support, send reproduction steps, expected/actual result, game and SKSE versions, Adorn/ASF versions, relevant outfit/NPC mods and screenshots. Include the relevant AdornLive.log from the active SKSE log directory; use the actual Skyrim Documents location, which may be redirected by Windows/OneDrive. Remove secrets and unrelated personal information from shared diagnostics."},{"title":"Troubleshooting Adorn","group":"Adorn","section":"Updates and backups","path":"adorn/troubleshooting.html#updates-and-backups","text":"## Updates and backups Before replacing runtime files, exit Skyrim and back up the saves/co-saves, Adorn Configs and Adorn-generated Overwrite files. Keep the release's DLL, UI and scripts together. Preserve personal JSON and generated assignment patches. ASF authors must also preserve their prepared ESP/SEQ/audio as a matching set. Current config reads prefer an existing file in Overwrite, then enabled Adorn Configs, before shipped defaults. Existing personal author data in Overwrite also keeps subsequent author writes/builds there. A blank Configs starter therefore does not erase or supersede existing Overwrite content. Review actual winning files before consolidating folders. See User data. For removal, back up first, retire unwanted assignments through the UI and verify restoration after restarting. Inspect generated Adorn files separately from runtime files. A return to a save made before installation is the clearest rollback; no clean mid-save uninstall guarantee is made."},{"title":"Troubleshooting Adorn","group":"Adorn","section":"Files and limits","path":"adorn/troubleshooting.html#files-and-limits","text":"## Files and limits | Data | Ownership | | --- | --- | | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/rules.json and drafts.json | Shared NPC/faction choices and working drafts | | SKSE/Plugins/SkyPatcher/{npc,outfit}/zzzzAdorn/zzAdornRules.ini | Shared generated next-launch rules | | Player saved looks | Current game's SKSE co-save | | Old player-outfits.json | Explicit recovery source only | | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/settings.json | Shared BodySlide output choice | | MCM/Settings/AdornSlots.ini | Local MCM bindings/author access | | Exported pack JSON | Chosen Save As location | | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/AssignmentPacks/ | Optional installed-pack library | Back up both saves/co-saves and shared configuration when moving installations. | Limit | Scope | | --- | --- | | 32 pieces | One custom look | | 64 custom slots | NPC/faction custom assignment bank; disabled rules reserve slots | | 512 groups / 4096 total recipients / 8 MB | Version 1 assignment pack | | 32 craftable piece slots | Separate ASF recipe system per save, not the NPC assignment bank | One imported source group shares a slot across accepted recipients. Installed plugin outfits use no custom slots. Replacement imports still need staging capacity; a full bank can require freeing space first. ### Import details Review is per recipient, so part of a mixed group can be accepted while the rest stays unchanged. Disabled contributions remain disabled. Identical assignments are skipped. Accepting an explicitly empty faction exclusion list clears the old exclusions for that contribution. Credit survives edits and re-export. Packs carry record references, not mod assets, original-outfit snapshots, runtime IDs or local allocation. Plugin renaming, FormID compaction or removed records can invalidate an old contribution. Use compatible defining mods and review dependencies again. A direct child contribution needs local preview/approval; contributor approval is not trusted as yours. Missing dependencies and blocked rows should be resolved through review, not guessed runtime IDs."},{"title":"Introduction to ASF","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"","path":"asf/introduction.html","text":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF) gives the outfits you choose in Adorn a place in your adventure—and gives authors the tools to create the character who provides them. Pick a look, find the assigned seller, solve their request and return with the answer items. Earn the finished pieces when enabled, or receive a named parchment and learn to craft the outfit yourself. A tailor, a demanding collector, or a follower with an unusual side business. ASF supplies the order and reward system; the author's choices give that service its personality, conversation and crafting rules."},{"title":"Introduction to ASF","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"An outfit worth working towards","path":"asf/introduction.html#an-outfit-worth-working-towards","text":"## An outfit worth working towards Start with an installed outfit or a custom combination assembled in Adorn. The first order points you towards the assigned NPC, and speaking through their outfit-planning dialogue introduces the seller before revealing the payment riddle. An authored request can require one to eight distinct miscellaneous items, with quantities that must all be satisfied. Bring the complete collection back to the seller for hand-in. The request belongs to the accepted order, so later author edits do not rewrite the deal you are already pursuing. With seller mode active, Adorn's ordinary direct-grant route gives way to ordering. Wearing a saved look checks that the player owns its pieces. The wardrobe remains convenient while acquiring its contents becomes part of play."},{"title":"Introduction to ASF","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"Craft the look you selected","path":"asf/introduction.html#craft-the-look-you-selected","text":"## Craft the look you selected ASF can generate native crafting entries for supported selected clothing and armour pieces even when their original mod supplies no crafting recipes. It uses Adorn-owned recipe slots without copying or editing the outfit mod's original recipes. The mods supplying the pieces still remain required. Recipe rewards arrive as distinct named parchments. Read the note to learn that outfit's entries, then collect its separate crafting materials. Previously learned outfits remain craftable as later orders are completed, within the shared 32 craftable-piece slots per save. Authors choose materials per piece, parchment instructions and optional named station locations. Armour normally uses a forge and clothing a tanning rack. They can also allow finished-outfit orders, which deliver the selected pieces directly and use no recipe slots."},{"title":"Introduction to ASF","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"Give a character the seller role","path":"asf/introduction.html#give-a-character-the-seller-role","text":"## Give a character the seller role Assign a placed NPC as the seller: an existing character, a suitable follower or someone supplied by a compatible content pack. The generic framework requires no particular follower, and the NPC does not need a merchant inventory for these orders. One seller is active at a time, while saved conversation drafts can cover several NPCs. The service's dialogue sits alongside the character's ordinary merchant, follower and quest conversations; it does not replace their entire voice or personality."},{"title":"Introduction to ASF","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"Write and perform the conversation","path":"asf/introduction.html#write-and-perform-the-conversation","text":"## Write and perform the conversation The in-game dialogue editor covers seven core seller exchanges, from opening the planner to hand-in, delivery and pending-order banter. Write the seller's reply, give the player compatible alternative prompts and save a draft for that NPC. For the performance, choose from 42 stock Skyrim voice styles with seven catalogued replies each—294 recording candidates. You can audition a reply before choosing it, seed a conversation from a style and replace individual moments. You can also record through a microphone inside Skyrim, import supported audio files and trim a selected take using its waveform. Mix stock recordings, your own performances and silent subtitle/lip replies across the conversation. The original takes stay available. The Build workflow generates the matching NPC-conditioned dialogue records, voice filenames, FUZ/lip files and supporting output. Authors prepare the conversation in game, let the build finish, then exit for installation and restart to activate changed dialogue. They do not manually create each dialogue record or calculate its audio filename."},{"title":"Introduction to ASF","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"Author the challenge","path":"asf/introduction.html#author-the-challenge","text":"## Author the challenge The riddle maker starts with real answer items and quantities. Write the initial riddle, optionally add an extra clue, and set deduction difficulty and acquisition effort separately. Prepare the extra clue as a recorded or silent native reply so a stuck player can ask the seller for help on their accepted order. Optional Easy, Medium and Hard reward tiers connect eligible riddles to classified reward pieces. Tiered offers are remembered within the save, preventing cancellation from repeatedly rerolling the same deal. Tiers are off by default; authors must supply and review a suitable progression pool. OpenRouter writing assistance is optional. It can suggest wording for the chosen answer items, which the author reviews and saves. Ordinary gameplay and manual authoring work offline. Players using prepared content need no API key."},{"title":"Introduction to ASF","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"For players and content authors","path":"asf/introduction.html#for-players-and-content-authors","text":"## For players and content authors Players can use a prepared seller setup and follow the order loop. NPC authors and modlist creators can configure the seller, write the conversation, record replies, choose recipe rules and build a pack for those players. ASF requires Adorn and its listed dependencies, plus its own runtime requirements. Authors building changed dialogue need the additional author tools; players using prepared output do not. The requirements guide separates the two roles. The compatibility and limits guide explains recipe capacity, the active seller role and the restart required after building changed dialogue."},{"title":"Your first seller order","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"","path":"asf/getting-started.html","text":"This is the player walkthrough for Adorn Seller Framework (ASF). With a prepared seller setup, you will choose a look in Adorn, meet the assigned character, solve the item payment and receive either finished pieces or a recipe to learn."},{"title":"Your first seller order","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"Requirements","path":"asf/getting-started.html#requirements","text":"## Requirements Players: Adorn with SKSE64, Address Library, Prisma UI and its requirements, SkyUI, MCM Helper and SkyPatcher; runtime-matched Fuz Ro D-oh; any NPC/content dependencies named by the seller pack. Follow Adorn's BodySlide and outfit-asset setup as well. Use MO2 for these instructions. Adorn and ASF have only been tested within an MO2 modlist on Windows. Other managers and installations outside MO2 are untested. Already included with ASF's complete author bundle: the self-contained dialogue compiler, FFmpeg and portable eSpeak NG/data. No additional copies of these tools or separate .NET SDK are needed for in-game Build. Install separately only when building changed dialogue/audio: Python 3 and the Creation Kit. LipGenerator, xwmaencode and LIPFuzer come from that CK installation; they are not separate ASF downloads. Players using prepared content need none of this authoring toolchain. Required for authors using stock Skyrim replies: download the BSArch command-line tool and place BSArch.exe at \\tools\\xEdit\\BSArch.exe. It is not bundled with ASF or the Creation Kit, and the xEdit editor itself is not required. ASF calls it automatically to extract the installed Skyrim - Voices_en0.bsa for stock recordings. See the BSArch setup instructions. Entirely silent or custom-audio-only setups do not use stock extraction. Already have xEdit/SSEEdit? BSArch is included with xEdit builds. Check for BSArch.exe in that installation before downloading it separately. If it is already in the required MO2 location, no additional installation is needed. ASF does not need you to run the xEdit editor. Manual riddle/recipe text editing needs no audio toolchain; preparing native Clue replies uses the dialogue build tools. OpenRouter is optional for writing drafts and unnecessary for gameplay or a manually authored build. See requirements for download links and exact author-tool paths."},{"title":"Your first seller order","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"Install the framework","path":"asf/getting-started.html#install-the-framework","text":"## Install the framework Install Adorn and its runtime requirements, then ASF and the runtime-matched Fuz Ro D-oh build. Enable AdornSlots.esp and Adorn Seller Framework.esp. Put the supplied personal configuration or authored output below the runtime mods in MO2's left pane, and check for existing Overwrite files with higher priority. The clean generic setup has no assigned NPC and seller mode is off. If your modlist supplies a seller pack, follow that pack's instructions and dependencies. Otherwise complete Author setup below. A particular follower is not a generic framework requirement."},{"title":"Your first seller order","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"Play an order","path":"asf/getting-started.html#play-an-order","text":"## Play an order 1. Press F6, choose an installed or custom look in Outfits, then open Assign → Player. 2. Choose Order recipe. If the author enabled finished pieces, Order outfit is also available. Name the order when asked. 3. On the first encounter, follow Find [seller's name]. Speak to the seller using the Adorn outfit-planning choice; simply standing nearby does not complete the introduction. The riddle is hidden until you speak to them. 4. Read the riddle in the Player order panel. Solve it and bring all answer items in the required quantities. The payment is an item hand-in, not a typed answer. 5. If offered, ask the seller for a Clue. It repeats an extra hint for this order and does not charge or change the payment. 6. Use the seller's hand-in choice. Adorn checks every required item before attempting payment. An incomplete collection should not receive a reward or partial payment deduction; report a failure with the exact items and quantities. 7. For a recipe, collect and read the named parchment. Then gather its separate crafting materials and use the correct station. For a finished outfit, the selected pieces are delivered directly. The exact dialogue wording may vary by authored pack. The NPC's normal merchant/follower dialogue remains separate."},{"title":"Orders, recipes & progression","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"","path":"asf/orders-and-recipes.html","text":"ASF keeps the selected reward, accepted payment and recipe information together as an order. This guide explains the two delivery routes, how learned crafting entries are retained, what belongs to your save and what encounter recovery preserves."},{"title":"Orders, recipes & progression","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"Recipes and finished outfits","path":"asf/orders-and-recipes.html#recipes-and-finished-outfits","text":"## Recipes and finished outfits | Order | What you receive | What remains to do | | --- | --- | --- | | Recipe | A named note teaching the selected outfit when read | Read it, collect the recipe materials and craft each piece. Armour uses a forge; clothing uses a tanning rack. Follow any named-location restriction on the parchment. | | Finished outfit | The selected pieces directly | Wear them or save the look. No recipe piece slots are consumed. | Riddle payment and crafting ingredients are separate costs. Recipe ingredients are specified per crafted piece. Recipe orders share 32 craftable piece slots per save; a multi-piece order uses capacity for its pieces. A completed recipe note must be read before its completed card is archived/replaced. Dropping a learned note does not unlearn it. ASF generates native crafting entries for the supported clothing/armour pieces in the chosen reward, including pieces whose original mod supplies no crafting recipe. It uses Adorn-owned recipe slots; it does not copy or edit the outfit mod's original recipes. No separate per-outfit recipe patch is needed for this route, but the mods supplying the reward pieces remain required. Previous learned outfits retain their entries when later orders are completed, within the same 32-piece capacity. Each recipe order has a distinct note identity. Its displayed page contains the outfit name, authored instructions, any named station-location restrictions and the seller's signature. Read the newly delivered note to learn that order; reading an older note does not substitute for it. Recipes-only mode hides/rejects new finished-outfit orders. Turning that setting on does not invalidate an already accepted outfit delivery."},{"title":"Orders, recipes & progression","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"Earning and wearing pieces","path":"asf/orders-and-recipes.html#earning-and-wearing-pieces","text":"## Earning and wearing pieces With seller mode enabled, Give and Wear on an unsaved selection reject direct grants and ask you to place an order. Wear on a saved look requires all its selected pieces to be in the player's inventory. It does not create missing pieces. Ordinary Adorn without seller/developer mode permits direct grants; enabling ASF's seller mode deliberately changes that player acquisition workflow."},{"title":"Orders, recipes & progression","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"Pending orders and fixed offers","path":"asf/orders-and-recipes.html#pending-orders-and-fixed-offers","text":"## Pending orders and fixed offers Accepted orders snapshot their riddle, requested items and recipe information. Editing shared content does not rewrite the accepted deal. Pending answer/debug details stay hidden, including with author tools unlocked. In tiered mode, an offer is remembered by seller, selected pieces, recipe/outfit type and classified tier within the current save. Cancelling or resetting the encounter does not reroll that offer. A new game has its own journal. Author rules that change the reward's tier create a different offer identity; changing rules is an author balance decision. The journal holds up to 512 distinct tiered offers and 64 recent-history entries; repeat avoidance looks at the last five IDs/families when alternatives exist. Hitting the offer limit reports an error. Legacy flat selection does not have the tiered fixed-offer guarantee."},{"title":"Orders, recipes & progression","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"Save, reset and recover","path":"asf/orders-and-recipes.html#save-reset-and-recover","text":"## Save, reset and recover | Shared setup across saves using the files | Personal progress in the loaded save | | --- | --- | | Assigned seller, enabled/options, dialogue drafts, selected recordings, prepared output, riddle/recipe pools, tier rules, NPC/faction assignments | Player saved looks, seller introduction/discovery, pending/completed order state, learned recipes, tiered offers/history | Save the game after personal changes and keep the matching .skse co-save. Loading an earlier save restores its earlier personal state. Starting a new game keeps authored setup but starts a fresh personal wardrobe and seller encounter. Using two characters with the same name does not intentionally share their personal progress. For recovery, use MCM → Adorn → Troubleshooting → Reset seller encounter…. Confirming restarts introduction/discovery and cancels this save's pending order. It keeps saved outfits, learned recipes, completed rewards and tiered offer prices. It does not clear the shared author configuration. Back up the save first and save again after the intended reset. Old shared wardrobes can be copied through Assign → Player → Saved outfits → Recover old saved outfits…. This is explicit recovery, not an automatic new-game import."},{"title":"Troubleshooting ASF","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"","path":"asf/troubleshooting.html","text":"ASF depends on the configured seller, the current save’s order state and the matching installed dialogue output. Use the symptom checks here to identify whether a problem belongs to setup, rewards, recording or a prepared build, and which details to include when asking for help."},{"title":"Troubleshooting ASF","group":"Adorn Seller Framework (ASF)","section":"Troubleshooting","path":"asf/troubleshooting.html#troubleshooting","text":"## Troubleshooting | Symptom | What to check | | --- | --- | | Seller controls absent | Confirm ASF ESP and matched core are loaded, then unlock author tools. Ordinary players normally use the Player order panel, not author setup. | | Seller mode inactive | Check the assigned placed reference, enabled setting and winning AdornSeller.json; existing Overwrite may override a blank starter. | | Still says Find seller | Speak through the outfit-planning dialogue. Reaching the marker alone does not introduce you. | | No finished-outfit option | The setup is recipes-only. Authors can enable finished orders in Seller setup. | | No eligible tier error | Add valid same-tier entries available at this level and order type. Check missing answer plugins. Save tier rules separately. | | Cancelling gives the same riddle | Expected for the same tiered offer. Encounter reset also preserves those prices. | | No Clue question | Check nonempty saved hint, matching assigned seller/order, completed introduction, exact prepared version and post-build restart. No-hint orders have no question. | | New reply does not play | Check Playing now versus Selected draft; build, exit/install and restart. Verify the authored output wins over the generic framework. | | Build cannot find a tool | Read publish-log.txt. Check Python and installed CK audio tools. Bundled eSpeak/FFmpeg must remain with their data/notices; stock sources can require BSArch and the local game's voice archive. | | Recipe not craftable | Read the delivered note first; check ingredients per piece, forge versus tanning rack, any location restriction and recipe capacity. | | Other NPC draft breaks Build | The publisher processes all saved drafts. Resolve its missing recording or tool requirement and rebuild. Preserve the draft/takes while diagnosing. | Report your versions, seller/base mod, order type, selected reward, save/new-game steps, expected versus actual result and relevant logs. Include the selected model and error for assistance failures, never the key."},{"title":"Introduction to author tools","group":"Author tools","section":"","path":"author/introduction.html","text":"Author tools let you create the content behind Adorn Seller Framework (ASF): the seller’s conversation, item-payment challenges, recipe rules and prepared audio. They are for NPC authors, modlist creators and players building their own setup. Players using a finished seller pack can follow its instructions without preparing new dialogue themselves. The tools work together. The seller gives the service a face, the conversation gives them a personality, the riddle defines the payment and the recipe defines what the player learns to craft. A prepared build connects the authored replies to native Skyrim dialogue."},{"title":"Introduction to author tools","group":"Author tools","section":"Begin with the seller","path":"author/introduction.html#begin-with-the-seller","text":"## Begin with the seller Read the ASF introduction to understand the player loop, then follow seller setup. Choose a reachable placed NPC, enable the service and decide whether to allow finished-outfit orders or keep the setup focused on recipes. Author access is unlocked through the MCM. It exposes configuration controls; it does not supply a new NPC, install the item dependencies or make a progression pool balanced automatically."},{"title":"Introduction to author tools","group":"Author tools","section":"Write the conversation and choose its performance","path":"author/introduction.html#write-the-conversation-and-choose-its-performance","text":"## Write the conversation and choose its performance The dialogue guide covers seven core exchanges and compatible alternative player prompts. Save separate drafts for the NPCs you author, with one active seller role at a time. For each exchange, choose a stock recording, a selected personal take or silent preparation. The recording guide explains microphone capture, audio imports, waveform trimming and matching the recorded words to the reply."},{"title":"Introduction to author tools","group":"Author tools","section":"Decide how rewards are crafted","path":"author/introduction.html#decide-how-rewards-are-crafted","text":"## Decide how rewards are crafted The recipe maker defines crafting materials per piece, parchment instructions and optional station locations. It supplies the rules used by new recipe orders; accepted orders retain their saved recipe. This is separate from the riddle payment. A player can first solve the seller’s request to earn the note, then gather the recipe’s own materials to make each piece."},{"title":"Introduction to author tools","group":"Author tools","section":"Build a fair challenge pool","path":"author/introduction.html#build-a-fair-challenge-pool","text":"## Build a fair challenge pool Start with the first-riddle guide. Select real answer items and quantities, then write a riddle that fairly points to them. The full riddle reference covers every field, the extra clue and the saved content format. If you want reward progression, review tiers and fixed offers before enabling the optional tier rules. Starter content is an example pool, not a balanced progression ready for every modlist. Writing assistance is optional. It offers suggestions for your chosen answers; you remain responsible for reviewing and saving the final wording."},{"title":"Introduction to author tools","group":"Author tools","section":"Prepare, test and share","path":"author/introduction.html#prepare-test-and-share","text":"## Prepare, test and share Use Build and share a seller to turn saved drafts into matching dialogue records and audio. Changed native dialogue requires the build, game exit, installation and restart sequence. Check the author requirements before building. Play through the seller’s conversation, hand-in, clues and rewards in Skyrim before distributing the setup, and confirm that their ordinary NPC dialogue is still available."},{"title":"Set up a seller","group":"Author tools","section":"","path":"asf/seller-setup.html","text":"An ASF setup gives one placed NPC the active seller role and defines which order routes players can use. This guide is for authors and modlist creators configuring that service before writing its conversation or building custom dialogue."},{"title":"Set up a seller","group":"Author tools","section":"Author setup","path":"asf/seller-setup.html#author-setup","text":"## Author setup 1. In MCM → Adorn → Developer access code, enter the author code supplied by the project/modlist author. After acceptance, Developer tools unlocked appears. Unlocking is a local authoring convenience, not a security boundary. 2. Open Seller → Setup → Choose seller from NPCs. Choose a placed NPC reference and confirm Assign as seller. If no placed reference resolves, load the NPC's area and try again; selecting a base record alone does not create an actor. 3. Enable seller mode. Choose whether to Allow finished outfit orders; off means recipes only. 4. Verify the assigned name, location and voice information. Keep the seller reachable in your intended playthrough. Use relocation controls only when you intend to move an actor/player in your test save. 5. Test one ordinary recipe order with the default replies before adding custom dialogue or tiers. The unlock persists through local MCM settings across saves/restarts. An empty code field does not mean locked: the field clears after use. Untick Developer tools unlocked to clear the saved credential and lock tools. Do not distribute your personal MCM settings file. One placed NPC holds the role at a time. Draft conversations are stored per NPC base and retained when switching sellers. A custom provider is matched to that base, so another placed reference of the same base can use its authored content. Switching sellers resets the custom-path preference for the new choice; check its own prepared state."},{"title":"Set up a seller","group":"Author tools","section":"Author workspace","path":"asf/seller-setup.html#author-workspace","text":"## Author workspace | View/control | Responsibility | | --- | --- | | Seller → Setup | Placed seller, enabled role and finished-order permission | | Seller → Dialogue | Per-NPC conversation, core exchanges, installed/draft state and build | | Use my prepared seller replies | Prefer installed NPC provider; generic path remains without valid output | | Edit default player choices | Generic fallback prompts, not a second editor for an existing custom conversation | | Author details | Effective VoiceType folder and future-seller template action | | Riddles | Payment, initial wording, extra clue/question, tiers and writing assistance | | Recipes | Parchment, materials per piece and station-location choices | | Assign → Player | Player orders and wardrobe | | MCM → Troubleshooting | Current-save encounter recovery | | Open build logs | Publisher diagnostics | Dialogue has four panes for seller/voice, exchanges, text/build state and audio. Left-stick focus moves between controls; left/right reaches same-row actions and adjacent panes. Long focused text can scroll before focus leaves. Browse a voice dropdown with up/down and close with Accept/Back. The mouse wheel scrolls hovered content. Riddles has its own four fixed panes; right-stick up/down scrolls its focused pane. ### Default choices and future-seller templates Edit default player choices edits fallback prompts while custom output is unavailable/inactive. It does not rewrite the selected seller's custom conversation. Save lines applies those choices to a subsequent eligible conversation; check Playing now. Under Author details, Use these player choices for future sellers copies only those prompts into the starting template. Existing NPC conversations remain unchanged. It does not clone recordings, reward logic or all sellers' text. ### Changing or disabling the seller Turning seller mode off retains the selected NPC and authored work. It is not a reset. Choosing another seller retains previous drafts, but only one placed actor is active. Check the new seller's prepared preference and voice folder. Inspect pending order snapshots before testing reassignment; a new seller should not be assumed to reprice or inherit an accepted deal."},{"title":"Write the conversation","group":"Author tools","section":"","path":"asf/dialogue.html","text":"ASF’s dialogue editor lets you give the seller their own player prompts and replies across seven core exchanges. This guide explains drafts, stock recording sources and voice folders so you can prepare a conversation while preserving the NPC’s ordinary dialogue."},{"title":"Write the conversation","group":"Author tools","section":"Write the seller dialogue","path":"asf/dialogue.html#write-the-seller-dialogue","text":"## Write the seller dialogue Open Seller → Dialogue. The summary Playing now → Selected draft → Next distinguishes installed replies from your edits. Each of the seven core exchanges has player choices and one seller reply. Put player choices on separate lines in What you say; they lead to the same reply for that exchange. Automatic delivery moments do not create extra menu choices. The framework's order/payment logic remains fixed. | Action | Result | | --- | --- | | Preview Skyrim recordings, Hear again, Stop | Listen only. Browsing does not choose a draft recording. | | Choose this reply and recording | Copy the exact stock reply and recording choice into the selected exchange. | | Choose [voice] for all 7 replies | Select that stock style for the seven core exchanges after confirmation. It does not voice every extra clue. | | Save draft | Persist the conversation and choices; installed playback stays as it was. | | Build [seller]'s seller dialogue | Save the draft, build records/audio and install after Skyrim exits. Restart to activate. | Editing a stock reply's words invalidates its exact stock recording choice; select another recording or use silent preparation. Borrowing Skyrim recordings for a custom-voice NPC also needs Build: having the source clip is not the same as having a seller-specific dialogue route. Prepared replies cover Adorn's seller exchanges. They do not replace the NPC's whole VoiceType or ordinary conversations. A preference for custom dialogue with no installed provider keeps the generic path active while the author works. ### The seven core exchanges | Exchange | Role | Writing guidance | | --- | --- | --- | | Opening / planner | Start planning through the seller | Welcome without claiming payment/delivery happened | | Hand-in | Offer collected answer items | Ask to check; native logic determines the result | | Missing items | Incomplete payment | Do not claim partial payment or reward | | Recipe delivery | Recipe success | Refer to receiving and reading the note | | Outfit delivery | Finished-piece success | Refer to finished pieces, not an unread recipe | | Leaving | Pending-order defer/leave | Keep compatible with an existing pending order | | Style banter | Pending-order flavour | Avoid inventing quest/payment mechanics | Leaving and style banter are pending-order gated. Automatic result moments are not arbitrary new menu branches. Clue replies are additional per-riddle versions authored through Riddles. All player alternatives in a moment lead to its one seller reply. Keep them compatible. A first-prompt fallback exists in the built records; rotation depends on matching runtime/provider state. ### Start and revise a draft Use Start with this voice's replies to seed a Skyrim style, or Start without Skyrim recordings for silent/custom work. Review replacement feedback and save wanted edits before restarting a draft. Mix stock, silent and recorded moments as needed. Undo edits since last save reloads saved draft choices; it does not uninstall the current prepared build. Current exchange in Skyrim expands the installed snapshot independently of the text being edited."},{"title":"Write the conversation","group":"Author tools","section":"Reply sources and voice folders","path":"asf/dialogue.html#reply-sources-and-voice-folders","text":"## Reply sources and voice folders The stock catalogue contains 42 Skyrim voice styles with seven core replies each: 294 recording candidates. Preview a clip before choosing it, choose a single exchange, or seed the seven core moments from one style and replace individual moments. Different exchanges can use different source styles or mix stock recordings with selected takes and silent replies. Audition the source clip, then check the finished reply on your chosen NPC after building and installing it. | State | Meaning | Next step | | --- | --- | --- | | Original/generic | Framework fallback handles the actor | Keep it or author a custom provider | | Stock chosen | Exact audited words/recording selected in draft | Build seller route, exit/install, restart | | Silent authored | Subtitle intended for silent FUZ/lip | Build, restart and test lips/subtitles | | Selected take | Source and trim bound to reply | Build into final output | | Staged FUZ | Converted audio/lip data exists | Finish installation/restart | | Installed provider | Required routing/records detected | Verify actual branches, sound and lips | Source style and final voice folder are distinct. A Skyrim style supplies recordings; the NPC's effective VoiceType determines where built FUZ files go. Borrowing a seller clip does not replace the NPC's ordinary voice or require changing it. Inspect Author details → NPC voice type used for the final audio. Pending/unresolved voice data prevents reliable placement. Correct only after checking the actor's winning voice. If an overhaul changes the VoiceType, rebuild/recheck the pack."},{"title":"Record, import & trim","group":"Author tools","section":"","path":"asf/recording.html","text":"Use this workflow to supply a seller reply with your own performance, either recorded in game or imported from an audio file. You will preview and trim the take, bind it to the intended words and prepare it for the matching dialogue build."},{"title":"Record, import & trim","group":"Author tools","section":"Record or import audio","path":"asf/recording.html#record-or-import-audio","text":"## Record or import audio Select an exchange and microphone device, then Record take → Stop & save. Alternatively place a WAV, FLAC, MP3, AAC or M4A in the displayed take folder and refresh. Preview, trim and choose the take. The original recording is retained; choosing a take normalizes audio for preparation. Review both the current subtitle and the words actually recorded. ASF does not transcribe speech automatically. For the seven core exchanges it can bind an intentional difference with a warning; lip generation follows recorded words. If the subtitle changes later, reselect the take to bind it again. Riddle clues are stricter: recorded words must match the saved extra clue. Raw take folders are author sources. Skyrim plays the built .fuz files in the final voice path, not an MP3/WAV dropped into a take folder. ### Trim and manage takes Select a take to display its waveform. Adjust Start and End, preview that range and keep complete words. Use selected take as audio saves the range for conversion/lips and retains the original source. Capture remains bound to the selected NPC/exchange until Stop & save. Finish capture before changing targets. Refresh devices after a hardware change, select the intended input and listen to a short test first. The reliable sequence is Refresh → select take → Preview take → trim → review spoken words → Use selected take as audio → Save draft → Build. Listening alone never chooses audio. Clearing the chosen take binding and deleting a source take are different operations. Back up useful recordings before deletion. A selected file that has gone missing is a build error, not an intentional silent choice."},{"title":"Record, import & trim","group":"Author tools","section":"Prepare an extra clue","path":"asf/recording.html#prepare-an-extra-clue","text":"## Prepare an extra clue 1. Assign the intended seller. In Riddles, save the initial riddle, extra clue and player's clue question. 2. Expand Clue dialogue & optional recording. For silent help, select Prepare clue dialogue. 3. For recorded help, choose Record / choose audio for this clue, select a matching take, then build through the normal ASF process. 4. Wait for Build complete, save and exit Skyrim. Allow installation to finish before restarting. 5. In game, ask the assigned seller for help on an accepted, discovered order. Confirm the words, subtitles, audio and actual lip movement match. Edit clue words/question in Riddles. The recorder is bound to that clue version. The builder retains archived help for older accepted orders; removing a pool entry does not intentionally replace an old order's help with a new riddle. Exact matching guards hide unavailable/stale help rather than offering the wrong reply. Silent preparation uses bundled eSpeak only as a temporary timing guide. The packaged reply is silent with lip data. This is not audible synthetic speech or neural TTS."},{"title":"Build & share a seller","group":"Author tools","section":"","path":"asf/build-and-share.html","text":"Saving a dialogue draft does not activate new replies in Skyrim. This guide takes authors through the build, exit, installation and restart sequence, then explains how to keep the matching files together in a seller pack for players."},{"title":"Build & share a seller","group":"Author tools","section":"Build and activate dialogue","path":"asf/build-and-share.html#build-and-activate-dialogue","text":"## Build and activate dialogue Authors need the author tools. Players using a finished pack do not. The builder creates the NPC-conditioned native dialogue records, correct INFO voice filenames, SEQ data, provider/voice manifests and prepared FUZ/lip files from saved drafts. Authors do not manually create each dialogue record or calculate its voice-file name. These generated files are a matching build and must stay together; preparing audio alone does not activate a new conversation. The bundled self-contained compiler avoids a separate .NET SDK requirement; Python and installed Creation Kit audio tools are still required as described above. 1. Review all saved NPC drafts, recordings and clue versions. The publisher builds saved drafts together, so another NPC's missing audio/tool dependency can fail the build. 2. Select Build [seller]'s seller dialogue or Prepare clue dialogue. Skyrim can remain open while preparation runs. 3. Wait for the result. On failure, use Open build logs; do not repeatedly rebuild without reading the error. 4. After the build completes, save and exit Skyrim. The publisher installs the checked records/audio after the process exits. Wait for installation/status to complete. 5. Check the winning ESP, SEQ, provider/voice manifests and FUZ output remain together in the intended user-data destination. Restart through SKSE and test the dialogue. Current writes use enabled Adorn Configs or Overwrite according to the user-data rules. Existing personal Overwrite content can keep the whole author output there. Do not clear it to force a different destination. For a failed build, Seller → Dialogue → Open build logs opens %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Nymph Nerds\\Adorn\\seller-build, selecting publish-log.txt if present. Use Alt+Tab if Explorer is behind Skyrim. If the log does not exist, the folder opens with an explanation. Keep the original error text and send the relevant log."},{"title":"Build & share a seller","group":"Author tools","section":"Share a finished seller setup","path":"asf/build-and-share.html#share-a-finished-seller-setup","text":"## Share a finished seller setup Use a clean authored configuration/output mod separate from Adorn and ASF. Include only the intended seller options, reviewed content, drafts or prepared files appropriate to the pack. Prepared ESP, SEQ, provider/voice manifests and FUZ files must describe the same build. Keep the authored output below the framework so it wins. List required NPC, answer-item and clothing plugins. JSON references do not install those mods. Test on an installation that lacks your private caches and recordings, and distinguish a finished player pack from source drafts that need building. Exclude personal saves, legacy player looks, unrelated assignment files, private MCM settings, credentials, unapproved takes and Local AppData caches. Do not redistribute locally extracted Skyrim clips or Creation Kit executables/data without permission. Preserve bundled tool notices and source obligations. Assignment-pack export does not export seller content."},{"title":"Recipe maker","group":"Author tools","section":"","path":"author/recipes.html","text":"Recipe templates define the crafting cost and instructions attached to new ASF recipe orders. This guide shows authors how to choose materials per reward piece, set station-location restrictions and test the delivered parchment and learned crafting entries."},{"title":"Recipe maker","group":"Author tools","section":"Author recipe templates","path":"author/recipes.html#author-recipe-templates","text":"## Author recipe templates Open Recipes with author tools unlocked: 1. Choose New recipe or a saved entry. Give it a name and write the parchment instructions. 2. Under Materials per piece, choose 1–8 distinct materials and quantities 1–99. These are crafting costs for each reward piece, not the riddle hand-in. 3. Keep All forges / All tanning racks for ordinary access, or choose a named location separately for each station type. Check in game that the location actually has the needed station. A location search result alone does not establish that. 4. Describe any location restriction clearly on the parchment. Select Save recipe. 5. Place a new recipe order, complete the hand-in, read the note, and craft both an armour and a clothing example at the intended stations. New orders choose a valid template from the pool. Accepted orders keep their saved recipe; changing a template is not a way to repair an already accepted order. Keep stable IDs when updating content and review defining-plugin dependencies before sharing. The material and location pickers search loaded game records and retain the required internal references. You do not need to enter FormIDs or author recipe JSON manually for this workflow. A named-location restriction controls the eligible station location; it does not place a missing forge or tanning rack in the world."},{"title":"First riddle","group":"Author tools","section":"","path":"author/first-riddle.html","text":"This quick start covers the fixed four-pane editor, tiered payments, extra clues and optional OpenRouter assistance. Detailed fields, JSON and troubleshooting: Riddle maker manual. Seller setup/voice builds: ASF guide."},{"title":"First riddle","group":"Author tools","section":"Make a riddle without AI","path":"author/first-riddle.html#make-a-riddle-without-ai","text":"## Make a riddle without AI 1. Unlock author tools in MCM → Adorn with the supplied author code. Open Riddles → New riddle. 2. In Answers & challenge, select Choose answer item and quantity. One item is enough. Use Add another required item for more: 1–8 distinct miscellaneous items, quantities 1–99 each. All are required together; cancelling an extra picker keeps earlier choices. 3. New entries start Easy. Set reward tier, clue difficulty and acquisition effort separately. Theme/family and access/delivery fields are under advanced settings. Availability prose guides writing; it creates no quest conditions. 4. In Writing & clue, write the initial Riddle and optional Seller's extra clue. Make every item/quantity fairly deducible without naming the answer. 5. Select Save riddle. Existing accepted orders and remembered tiered offers keep their original terms. The four panes are library, answers/challenge, writing/clue and Assistance. There is one shared draft. Controller right-stick up/down scrolls the focused pane; shoulder buttons change panes. Accept selects a dropdown item; Back closes its list."},{"title":"First riddle","group":"Author tools","section":"Get optional writing suggestions","path":"author/first-riddle.html#get-optional-writing-suggestions","text":"## Get optional writing suggestions 1. In rightmost Assistance → Set up assistance, save your own OpenRouter key and select a free, paid or custom model. Dots and Key saved confirm local Windows storage, not account validity. The real input clears. Remove key deletes it. 2. Model, writing voice and provider-data preference autosave for the same Windows account/PC. Wait for saved-status feedback. Preferences and the separate key are outside mods, saves and exports. 3. Choose real items, quantities and Easy/Medium/Hard. Missing prerequisites appear together. No required Review/JSON step exists; What is sent optionally explains context. 4. Select Generate suggestions (uses API credit) once. Model selection alone sends no request. Pending feedback and Cancel generation appear; a sent request may still cost credit after cancellation. 5. Browse Suggestion 1 of 3. Use riddle, Use extra clue or Use both copies only that wording into the shared editor. Combine alternatives and edit, then Save riddle yourself. Applying does not save or make another request. Manual wording edits keep alternatives; answer/profile changes clear obsolete ones. Late replies are rejected after context changes. Errors preserve your draft and saved pool. Requests send answer names/quantities, profile/tier-rule context, persona and writing facts to OpenRouter and its provider. Existing riddle/hint/question wording, FormIDs, paths, saves and recordings are excluded. The key authenticates the request. Keep private information out of free-text context. Allow providers that may store or train on writing requests defaults off. Enable only if you intend that broader policy; account restrictions still apply. Free capacity and structured-output support vary, with no paid fallback. See assistance details."},{"title":"First riddle","group":"Author tools","section":"Enable a balanced tier pool","path":"author/first-riddle.html#enable-a-balanced-tier-pool","text":"## Enable a balanced tier pool 1. Save reviewed entries in all three tiers. Existing entries remain Unclassified; tiers are off by default. 2. Expand library Tier settings. Review coverage/thresholds, enable tiered selection, then Save tier rules. Saving one riddle does not enable tiers. 3. Test every allowed delivery type at the lowest supported level. Minimum-level/delivery filtering applies only in tier mode. Unclassified entries do not fill classified buckets. Default classification uses total base armour and strongest piece: Medium at 40 total or 20 on one piece; Hard at 80 total or 40 on one piece. Zero-armour clothing defaults Easy. Skills, temporary effects and decorative piece count add no cost. Enchantment power/prestige are not inferred: calibrate and add minimum-tier overrides as needed. Missing eligible coverage stops the new order and preserves the current one. Recent IDs/families are avoided when alternatives exist. Same seller + pieces + order type + classified tier keeps its accepted offer within the save, including after cancellation/reset. Limits are 512 distinct offers and 64 history entries."},{"title":"First riddle","group":"Author tools","section":"Prepare an extra clue","path":"author/first-riddle.html#prepare-an-extra-clue","text":"## Prepare an extra clue 1. Assign the intended seller. Save the extra clue/question in Riddles. 2. Expand Clue dialogue & optional recording. Choose Prepare clue dialogue for silent subtitles/lip data, or Record / choose audio for this clue for a take matching the saved hint. 3. Use normal ASF Build. After Build complete, save, exit Skyrim, allow installation to finish, then restart. Python/installed CK audio tools remain author requirements; portable eSpeak and FFmpeg are bundled. 4. Ask for help on a pending, discovered order. Exact prepared help must match seller/order. Repeating it charges nothing and does not reroll. No hint or stale preparation means no Clue question. Edit words in Riddles. Archived prepared versions support earlier accepted orders; preserve matching output when updating. No recording is required. Silent preparation packages silence/lip data, not audible generated speech."},{"title":"First riddle","group":"Author tools","section":"Check your authored content","path":"author/first-riddle.html#check-your-authored-content","text":"## Check your authored content Use a backup save and check first-order Find [seller], complete/incomplete hand-ins, both delivery types, save/reload, fixed offers, archived hints and two-seller isolation. Start a genuine New Game to check fresh personal progress with shared setup retained. For recovery use MCM → Adorn → Troubleshooting → Reset seller encounter…; it preserves outfits, learned recipes, completed rewards and fixed prices. Check silent and recorded clues in Skyrim, including actual mouth movement. Manual writing/gameplay must work without a key. For assistance, test errors, cancellation and changing an answer while a reply is pending. Never send your key."},{"title":"Riddle maker reference","group":"Author tools","section":"","path":"author/riddles.html","text":"Create an item payment first, then write a fair riddle that points to it. The current editor supports manual writing, optional OpenRouter suggestions, reward tiers, and an extra clue spoken or subtitled by the assigned seller. For a shorter walkthrough, use the quick start. Seller setup, recordings and recipe authoring are covered by the ASF guide."},{"title":"Riddle maker reference","group":"Author tools","section":"Open the editor","path":"author/riddles.html#open-the-editor","text":"## Open the editor Unlock author tools through MCM → Adorn → Developer access code using the code supplied by the project/modlist author, then open Riddles. The code is a convenience gate. The accepted unlock persists in local MCM settings; the input clears after use. Untick Developer tools unlocked to lock it again. Four panes remain visible throughout editing: | Pane | Use it for | | --- | --- | | Riddle library | Select, search or create an entry; expand pool-wide Tier settings | | Answers & challenge | Payment items, quantities, tier, difficulty, effort and access/delivery metadata | | Writing & clue | Initial riddle, extra clue, clue dialogue and Save riddle | | Assistance | Optional key/model setup, writing voice, suggestions and apply controls | There is one shared writing draft. Assistance does not replace it. Advanced sections collapse within their panes, and dropdowns open below their field. With a controller, move focus with the left stick/D-pad and change panes with shoulder buttons. Right-stick up/down scrolls the focused pane. Accept chooses a menu item; Back closes it. Scroll long writing/expanded settings inside their pane, including at enlarged text sizes."},{"title":"Riddle maker reference","group":"Author tools","section":"Make your first riddle","path":"author/riddles.html#make-your-first-riddle","text":"## Make your first riddle 1. Choose New riddle from the library. 2. Select Choose answer item. Search loaded miscellaneous items by name, EditorID or plugin and choose the exact item. Set its quantity beside the selector. 3. Keep one item for the first test. Add another required item appears after the first choice; every listed item is required together. Cancelling an additional picker keeps earlier choices. 4. New entries start Easy. Set clue difficulty and acquisition effort to reflect your payment. 5. Write the Riddle in Writing & clue. Explain quantity fairly without naming the answer. Add an optional Seller's extra clue that narrows the answer without simply giving it away. 6. Select Save riddle and read the result. Adorn supplies an internal ID for a new entry. 7. Test on a new offer with a collectable answer. Existing accepted orders and remembered tiered offers keep their terms. For one iron ingot, an initial clue might be: “Drawn from stone and tempered by fire, I wait for the smith's next design. Bring one.” An extra clue might be: “Look for a common metal already cast into a bar.” This is a writing exercise, not a balance recommendation. Ask someone who has not seen the answer whether it points to the intended material rather than several metals. Sharpen ambiguous wording before release."},{"title":"Riddle maker reference","group":"Author tools","section":"Understand the fields","path":"author/riddles.html#understand-the-fields","text":"## Understand the fields | Field | Meaning and behavior | | --- | --- | | Answer item / Quantity | Exact MISC record and count consumed at hand-in; 1–8 distinct items, 1–99 of each | | Reward tier | Matches this payment to an Easy/Medium/Hard reward when tiers are enabled; Unclassified supports legacy content | | Clue difficulty | 1 direct, 2 some deduction, 3 subtle. Does not automatically change reward tier | | Acquisition effort | 1 accessible, 2 collection/travel, 3 substantial effort. Does not inspect rarity or quest access | | Theme | Writing context, such as metalwork or wilderness | | Answer family | Shared label such as ingots used to reduce related answers in tier mode; use consistent spelling/case | | Minimum player level | Tier-mode eligibility, from 1–1000 | | Order type | Tier-mode eligibility for recipe, finished outfit or both | | Verified availability / writing facts | Facts for writing/assistance. Prose creates no quest, faction, location or inventory condition | | Riddle | Initial player-facing wording; JSON calls this clue | | Seller's extra clue | Optional help reply; JSON calls this profile.hint | | Player's clue question | Prompt leading to help; defaults to “Could you give me a clue?” | | Internal riddle ID | Stable unique identity. Keep stable for updates; do not reuse for unrelated content | Tier, difficulty and effort are separate decisions. A cryptic clue for a common object is not automatically an expensive payment. A rare answer is not accessible just because its wording is obvious. | Text | Maximum UTF-8 bytes | | --- | --- | | Internal ID | 80 | | Initial riddle | 500 | | Extra clue | 300 | | Player clue question | 80, nonempty | | Theme / family | 80 each | | Availability facts | 500 | | Assistance writing voice | 1000 | Native validation counts UTF-8 bytes. Accented text, emoji and some punctuation use several bytes per character; shorten text if a visually short entry is rejected."},{"title":"Riddle maker reference","group":"Author tools","section":"Use tiers deliberately","path":"author/riddles.html#use-tiers-deliberately","text":"## Use tiers deliberately ### Legacy mode Tiers are off by default. Entries without profiles remain Unclassified. With tiers off, Adorn randomly chooses valid loaded entries; profile tier, minimum-level and order-type filters and recent-family avoidance are not applied. Setting one entry to Hard does not enable the pool-wide system. The three starter ingot riddles are functional examples, not a complete tiered economy. ### Enable tier selection 1. Save reviewed Easy, Medium and Hard entries. Include alternatives rather than one repetitive answer per tier. 2. Expand Tier settings in the library. Review coverage and thresholds. 3. Check Use tiered selection for new orders, then Save tier rules. This is separate from Save riddle. 4. Test every tier at the lowest supported level for each allowed order type. Basic coverage cannot prove every combination is eligible. Unclassified entries do not fill a classified bucket. Missing same-tier content stops the new order with an explanation and preserves the current order, rather than substituting an easier bucket. ### How rewards are classified The classifier counts each distinct selected reward record once, using its base armour rating. It considers total rating and the strongest individual piece. Skills, temporary effects and the player's worn armour total are excluded. | Default condition | Minimum tier | | --- | --- | | Total at least 80, or any one piece at least 40 | Hard | | Otherwise, total at least 40, or any one piece at least 20 | Medium | | Otherwise | Easy | | Total base armour is zero | Configured clothing tier, Easy by default | | Explicit piece override | At least the override tier | With defaults, a single 20-rating piece is Medium; a single 40-rating piece is Hard; four distinct 10-rating pieces total 40 and are Medium. Zero-rating accessories add no piece-count fee. A prestigious zero-armour robe is ordinary clothing unless you review its override or clothing rule. Enchantment strength, prestige, armour class, monetary value and quest access are not inferred. Calibrate for the modlist. Hard total and strongest-piece thresholds must each exceed their Medium equivalents. ### Exceptional piece overrides Expand Exceptional piece overrides under Tier settings. For example: ~~~json [{\"plugin\":\"Example.esp\",\"local\":2048,\"tier\":\"hard\"}] ~~~ This sets a floor for hexadecimal local FormID 000800, expressed here as decimal 2048. Override local is a decimal number; answer localFormId is a six-digit hexadecimal string. Neither uses the runtime load-order prefix. Overrides raise floors, not discount stronger rewards. Supported tiers are easy, medium, hard; up to 2000 distinct overrides are accepted. Use the actual defining plugin and valid piece in your installation. ### Repeats and accepted offers Tier mode avoids the last five riddle IDs and nonempty answer-family labels when eligible alternatives exist. If all candidates are recent, it reuses eligible content. A varied pool makes this useful. Accepted tiered offers are remembered by seller, set of reward pieces, order type and classified tier within the save. Reordering pieces, cancellation and encounter reset do not reroll the price. A new game starts empty. Changing author rules so a reward changes tier creates a different offer identity. Up to 512 distinct offers and 64 history entries are retained. A new distinct offer at the limit reports an error. Accepted wording/items remain snapshots after pool edits or deletion."},{"title":"Riddle maker reference","group":"Author tools","section":"Prepare the seller's extra clue","path":"author/riddles.html#prepare-the-sellers-extra-clue","text":"## Prepare the seller's extra clue The initial riddle in the order panel and a compiled seller help reply are separate. Saving text does not install dialogue. 1. Assign the intended seller and save a nonempty extra clue. 2. Expand Clue dialogue & optional recording in Writing & clue and review the question. 3. For silent help, select Prepare clue dialogue. ASF builds the seven core exchanges plus authored clues, with silent audio/lip data using its bundled timing guide. 4. For voiced help, select Record / choose audio for this clue. Record/import, trim, preview and choose a take matching the saved hint. Edit wording in Riddles, not the recorder. 5. Use normal ASF Build. After Build complete, save, exit Skyrim, allow installation to finish, then restart. 6. Ask the assigned seller for help on a pending, discovered order. Check words, sound, subtitles and actual mouth movement, including after save/reload. Only exact matching prepared help is offered for that seller/order. No hint means no question. Asking repeats the accepted hint without payment, rerolling or order progression. Missing/stale help hides the option rather than playing another hint. Archived prepared versions support earlier accepted orders after edits/deletion. Preserve matching records, manifests and audio when updating. Reselect recorded audio after wording changes to bind the new clue version. Silent preparation needs the ASF author dependencies. eSpeak makes a temporary timing guide; its speech is not packaged. Live AI conversation, voice cloning and neural TTS are outside this workflow."},{"title":"Riddle maker reference","group":"Author tools","section":"Optional OpenRouter assistance","path":"author/riddles.html#optional-openrouter-assistance","text":"## Optional OpenRouter assistance ### Set up once Under Assistance → Set up assistance, save your own key and choose a Free/Paid recommendation or custom Model ID. Model selection alone sends no generation request. Use a dedicated key with an account-side credit limit. The real input clears after saving. Dots and Key saved confirm local storage, not account validity/credit. Replace key changes it; Remove key deletes it. Model, writing voice and provider preference autosave; wait for saved-status feedback. Key and preferences use separate Windows Credential Manager entries for the same Windows user/PC. They survive restarts and are outside mods, exports and saves. Sharing Configs does not configure someone else's key/model. Relocking author tools is separate from Remove key. Choose a model/provider supporting the structured-output request; plain chat/JSON support alone is insufficient. Free listings do not guarantee capacity. See OpenRouter structured outputs. Prices/endpoints can change. ### Generate and combine 1. Choose real answer items/quantities, a classified tier, saved key and model. Missing prerequisites are listed together. Manual Unclassified entries remain supported. 2. Optionally set Seller's writing voice and checked availability facts. What is sent gives a readable summary; no required Review gate or raw JSON step exists. 3. Select Generate suggestions (uses API credit) once. Pending feedback and Cancel generation show the state. Errors preserve the editor and saved pool. 4. Use Suggestion 1 of 3 to compare. Use riddle replaces initial wording only; Use extra clue replaces the hint only; Use both changes both. Other fields stay intact. 5. Mix alternatives and edit manually, then Save riddle yourself. Applying never saves or sends another request. Manual wording edits and background pool refreshes keep alternatives. Answer/profile context changes clear obsolete alternatives. Wording edits invalidate an outstanding result so a late reply cannot apply to a newer draft. Cancel ignores the result; a request already sent may still consume credit. ### What leaves the PC | Sent as writing context | Excluded from writing context | | --- | --- | | Item display names/quantities; tier, difficulty, effort, theme/family, level/delivery metadata; availability facts; writing voice; tier-rule summary | Existing riddle/hint/question text; FormIDs and answer plugin references; exceptional-piece registry; paths, saves and recordings | The key is sent for authentication outside the writing prompt. OpenRouter and its selected provider receive the request. Free-text fields are sent as written: do not put private information into facts/persona. Allow providers that may store or train on writing requests defaults off and persists when changed. Enabling broadens routing for the selected model, without switching free to paid; account restrictions still apply. The stricter default is a provider-policy filter, not an independent guarantee about a provider's actual handling. See OpenRouter provider policies."},{"title":"Riddle maker reference","group":"Author tools","section":"Edit JSON outside the game","path":"author/riddles.html#edit-json-outside-the-game","text":"## Edit JSON outside the game Back up first. Personal content is at SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/AdornRiddles.json under the resolved Configs/Overwrite root. Shipped fallback is SKSE/Plugins/AdornRiddles.json. Existing personal Overwrite files win; see User data. Author saves write personal content, not the runtime default. Keep top-level \"version\": 1 and a riddles array. tierRules and entry profile are optional for legacy files. This complete example leaves tiers off because one entry cannot cover all tiers: ~~~json { \"version\": 1, \"tierRules\": { \"version\": 1, \"enabled\": false, \"mediumArmor\": 40, \"hardArmor\": 80, \"mediumPiece\": 20, \"hardPiece\": 40, \"clothingTier\": \"easy\", \"overrides\": [] }, \"riddles\": [ { \"id\": \"smiths_iron_01\", \"clue\": \"Drawn from stone and tempered by fire, I wait for the smith's next design. Bring one.\", \"requests\": [ {\"plugin\":\"Skyrim.esm\",\"localFormId\":\"05ACE4\",\"count\":1} ], \"profile\": { \"tier\": \"easy\", \"difficulty\": 1, \"effort\": 1, \"theme\": \"metalwork\", \"family\": \"ingots\", \"minLevel\": 1, \"delivery\": \"both\", \"access\": \"Verify ordinary smith access in the target modlist before release.\", \"hint\": \"Look for a common metal already cast into a bar.\", \"question\": \"Could you give me a clue?\" } } ] } ~~~ The older single-item format is still accepted as an entry's payment property: ~~~json {\"request\":{\"plugin\":\"Skyrim.esm\",\"localFormId\":\"05ACE4\",\"count\":1}} ~~~ Use requests for new entries, including single-item entries. Do not specify both: requests wins. For multiple items add distinct records; raise count instead of repeating one record. Use the defining plugin and six local hex digits including leading zeroes. Runtime IDs are not portable. Invalid/unloaded answers, duplicate items, malformed text/profiles and duplicate valid IDs can make entries unavailable. A broken document or no valid entries prevents selection. Reload file explicitly replaces the active editor from disk; save/copy an unsaved draft first. External edits do not rebuild compiled clues automatically."},{"title":"Riddle maker reference","group":"Author tools","section":"Review and share","path":"author/riddles.html#review-and-share","text":"## Review and share Before shipping, check: - A tester can identify every exact answer without debug data, and quantities are fairly communicated. - Acquisition is possible at the supported level in the intended modlist. Test quest access rather than assuming a prose note enforces it. - Tier reflects practical cost; difficulty/effort labels do not balance automatically. - Extra hints help and match prepared audio/subtitles. - All three tiers work at supported levels and for both allowed delivery types. - Incomplete hand-ins remove nothing; complete ones give exactly the intended reward. Test save/reload, cancellation, archived clues and another seller. Collect contributor entries/JSON, review IDs/dependencies and merge into a clean content mod. Sharing a code does not synchronize installations or update a built modlist. Assignment-pack exports exclude riddles. Keep personal settings, keys, takes and unrelated configuration out of content-only packs."},{"title":"Riddle maker reference","group":"Author tools","section":"Troubleshooting","path":"author/riddles.html#troubleshooting","text":"## Troubleshooting | Symptom | Check or action | | --- | --- | | Item unavailable | Payment supports loaded MISC records. Check the defining plugin and use the active-game picker. | | Short-looking text rejected | UTF-8 byte limits can be reached before the visible character count. | | Tiers cannot enable | Save valid Easy/Medium/Hard entries, then test level/delivery coverage. | | Restricted entry appears with tiers off | Legacy selection ignores profile filters; enable a reviewed tier pool to use them. | | No eligible Hard payment | Check tier entries, answer plugins, minimum level and delivery. Fill missing content rather than discounting the reward. | | Same riddle after cancel/reset | Expected for the same tiered offer. Test a different offer or new test game. | | Clue question missing | Save exact wording, prepare for this seller, finish Build/exit/install/restart; check the accepted snapshot. | | Key saved but Generate unavailable | Review item, classified-tier and model prerequisites. Stored does not mean account-valid. | | Privacy rejection / no compatible route | Check structured-output support and model/account policy. Broader provider permission is a deliberate choice, not a guaranteed fix. | | Rate limit | Wait for capacity or intentionally choose another route. Repeated retries cannot create free capacity. | | Output budget / incomplete drafts | No complete three-draft response arrived. Continue manually or deliberately try another compatible model. | | Bad key / credit | Check the account and replace/remove the key in Assistance. Never send it in a report. | Reports should include model/error text, seller, delivery type, items/quantities, expected tier and save/new-game steps. Build errors also need publish-log.txt from Seller → Dialogue → Open build logs."},{"title":"Tiers & fixed offers","group":"Author tools","section":"","path":"author/tiers.html","text":"Reward tiers let authors connect the pieces being ordered to an appropriate pool of item-payment riddles. This guide explains how to prepare coverage, enable the optional rules and understand why an accepted tiered offer keeps its price within the save."},{"title":"Tiers & fixed offers","group":"Author tools","section":"Author riddles and tiers","path":"author/tiers.html#author-riddles-and-tiers","text":"## Author riddles and tiers Use the quick start for a first entry and the full riddle manual for every field, tier calculation, JSON examples and troubleshooting. Choose payment items first, write the initial riddle and optional extra clue, then Save riddle. Old entries remain Unclassified. New entries start Easy. Enabling tier selection is a separate pool-wide action under Tier settings → Save tier rules; it does not happen when you classify one riddle. The starter pool contains three legacy ingot riddles. It is deliberately not a balanced Easy/Medium/Hard progression. Build and test eligible content in all three tiers, at the lowest supported level and for both allowed order types, before enabling tiers for players."},{"title":"Tiers & fixed offers","group":"Author tools","section":"Riddle maker and tier configuration","path":"author/tiers.html#riddle-maker-and-tier-configuration","text":"## Riddle maker and tier configuration Choose Riddles → New riddle. The library, Answers & challenge, Writing & clue and rightmost Assistance remain visible. There is one draft and one Save riddle action. 1. Choose the exact loaded MISC answer and quantity. 2. Add another required answer only when it adds a fair challenge. All 1–8 distinct items are needed together, quantities 1–99 each. 3. Set reward tier, clue difficulty and acquisition effort separately. New entries start Easy; legacy entries stay Unclassified. 4. Add theme/family, optional minimum level and delivery type, and checked availability facts. Prose does not enforce quest/faction access. 5. Write the initial riddle and separate optional extra clue/question. Save, then prepare native help if used. Initial text has a 500 UTF-8-byte limit; extra clue 300; question 80; ID/theme/family 80 each; availability facts 500. Multibyte text can reach limits before its visible character count. ### Enabling tiers Tiers default off. Flat mode chooses valid loaded entries without tier/level/delivery filters. To enable, save reviewed content in all three buckets, open Tier settings, check Use tiered selection for new orders, then Save tier rules. Default reward classification counts each distinct selected record's base armour. Medium starts at 40 total or 20 on the strongest piece; Hard at 80 total or 40 on one piece. Zero-armour clothing defaults Easy, with a configurable clothing tier. Exceptional-piece overrides raise minimum tiers. Skills, temporary effects, decorative piece count, enchantment power, price and prestige are not inferred. Calibrate thresholds/overrides for the actual modlist. A powerful zero-armour robe needs author review. Difficulty and acquisition effort are ratings, not automatic tier calculation. Minimum level and recipe/outfit eligibility apply in tier mode. Test every tier at the lowest supported level for every allowed delivery type; a three-bucket coverage count alone cannot prove eligibility. Missing coverage stops the new offer and preserves the existing order. Recent-ID/family avoidance relaxes if all candidates are recent. Accepted tiered prices persist as described earlier. Use the riddle reference for all field/schema details and a complete JSON example. Keep IDs unique and stable; do not use a runtime load-order prefix as a portable answer reference."},{"title":"Optional writing assistance","group":"Author tools","section":"","path":"author/assistance.html","text":"OpenRouter is an optional writing aid for authors who have already chosen the real answer items and quantities. This guide explains how to request suggestions, review and apply their wording, and manage local key and preference storage; ordinary gameplay and manual writing need no API key."},{"title":"Optional writing assistance","group":"Author tools","section":"OpenRouter author assistance","path":"author/assistance.html#openrouter-author-assistance","text":"## OpenRouter author assistance This optional author tool drafts saved writing. It never runs when the player asks the seller for help and does not choose rewards, FormIDs or payment quantities. 1. Under Assistance → Set up assistance, save a dedicated limited-credit key. The input clears; saved dots confirm Windows storage, not account validity. 2. Choose a Free/Paid recommendation or custom Model ID supporting structured outputs. Selecting a model sends no inference request. 3. Set optional writing voice and checked availability facts. Model/persona/provider preference autosave; wait for confirmation. 4. Choose real answers/quantities and Easy/Medium/Hard. Missing prerequisites appear together. What is sent is optional readable context, with no mandatory Review/JSON step. 5. Select Generate suggestions (uses API credit). Read pending/error feedback. Cancellation ignores a result but can still leave a sent request billable. 6. Review Suggestion 1 of 3 and apply Use riddle, Use extra clue or Use both. Mix alternatives and edit manually, then Save riddle explicitly. Applying never saves or sends another request. Wording edits retain suggestions; answer/profile changes clear obsolete ones. Context changes invalidate pending results. Requests contain chosen item names/quantities, profile/tier-rule summary, persona and availability facts. Existing riddle/hint/question text, answer FormIDs/plugin references, piece-override registry, local paths, saves and recordings are excluded. The key authenticates outside the writing prompt. Free-text facts/persona go as written. Key and preferences are separate Windows Credential Manager entries for the same account/PC. They are excluded from Configs, saves and exports. Remove key deletes the key explicitly; relocking tools is separate. Provider data collection is disallowed by Adorn's default routing preference. Allow providers that may store or train on writing requests broadens it deliberately; account policy can still restrict routing. Free availability and compatible structured-output routes vary. There is no paid fallback. See provider policies and structured outputs. Manual writing and gameplay need no API key or internet. If a provider rejects a request, read the displayed error; your manual draft remains available."},{"title":"Introduction to the reference","group":"Reference","section":"","path":"reference/introduction.html","text":"The reference section explains how Adorn and Adorn Seller Framework (ASF) store their data, which files belong together, and which limits affect your setup. Use it when backing up an installation, investigating configuration priority or packaging authored content. If you are learning either mod for the first time, start with the Adorn introduction or ASF introduction. The task guides explain the workflow; the reference gives the supporting file and implementation detail."},{"title":"Introduction to the reference","group":"Reference","section":"Saves, configuration and backups","path":"reference/introduction.html#saves-configuration-and-backups","text":"## Saves, configuration and backups Saves, config and backups separates shared setup from progress belonging to the loaded save. It explains Adorn Configs and Overwrite priority, where authoring creates files, and why a game save and its matching SKSE co-save should be preserved together. Use that distinction before moving an installation or sharing a configuration. A seller setup and prepared voice output are not the same thing as a player’s order history, learned recipes or personal wardrobe."},{"title":"Introduction to the reference","group":"Reference","section":"Files, capacity and prepared output","path":"reference/introduction.html#files-capacity-and-prepared-output","text":"## Files, capacity and prepared output Files and limits identifies ASF’s drafts, recording sources, build manifests and final voice files. Prepared ESP, sequence data, provider information and audio describe a matching build and should stay together. Adorn’s separate files and limits cover the assignment bank and sharing capacity. Assignment slots and ASF’s per-save craftable-piece slots serve different purposes."},{"title":"Introduction to the reference","group":"Reference","section":"Author content formats","path":"reference/introduction.html#author-content-formats","text":"## Author content formats The riddle maker reference documents the content fields and JSON used for externally edited riddles. Keep stable entry IDs when updating a shared collection. The file format’s version identifies its schema, separately from the mod’s release version."},{"title":"Introduction to the reference","group":"Reference","section":"Credits and compatibility","path":"reference/introduction.html#credits-and-compatibility","text":"## Credits and compatibility Artwork and credits identifies the supplied v4 wordmark and heading font used by this wiki. Compatibility and limits covers supported installation guidance, content requirements and capacity. When asking for help, include the versions, steps, expected result, actual result and relevant logs so the problem can be reproduced."},{"title":"Saves, config & backups","group":"Reference","section":"","path":"reference/user-data.html","text":"Adorn keeps authored configuration separate from runtime defaults. On MO2, current reads prefer an existing per-file override in Overwrite, then enabled Adorn Configs, before shipped defaults. If overwrite/SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/ already contains personal author data, subsequent author saves/builds stay together in Overwrite. Otherwise an enabled, existing Adorn Configs mod is the write destination; without it, writes use Overwrite. A blank starter does not supersede personal Overwrite files. Files appear when their feature is first saved. mods/Adorn Configs/SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/ When Overwrite is the resolved destination, replace mods/Adorn Configs/ with overwrite/ in every path below. Files are created when their feature saves, not all at startup. Keep this mod's exact name Adorn Configs for the current resolver. Inspect winning files before moving content; preserve existing work. | Author data | Path below Adorn Configs or Overwrite | | --- | --- | | Assignments and drafts | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/rules.json, drafts.json | | Optional installed assignment packs | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/AssignmentPacks/.json (normal Import/Export uses files chosen anywhere through Open/Save) | | Old shared player outfits (recovery only) | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/player-outfits.json; new personal wardrobes live in each SKSE co-save | | Seller and edited content | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/AdornSeller.json, AdornRiddles.json, AdornRecipes.json, AdornSellerDialogue.json | | Per-NPC dialogue drafts | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/AdornSellerAuthorDrafts.json | | Raw takes, reply bindings, chosen take and trim | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/AdornSellerAuthorRecordings//takes// | | BodySlide output-folder choice | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/settings.json | | Generated assignment patches | SKSE/Plugins/SkyPatcher/{npc,outfit}/zzzzAdorn/zzAdornRules.ini | | Seller build request and results | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/publish-job.json, publish-status.json, AdornSellerProviders.json, AdornSellerVoiceJobs.json | | Prepared seller records and audio | Adorn Seller Framework.esp, SEQ/Adorn Seller Framework.seq, Sound/Voice/Adorn Seller Framework.esp//.fuz | | MCM settings | MCM/Settings/AdornSlots.ini (written by MCM Helper; Overwrite fallback needs an in-game check) | It holds outfit assignments (rules.json), the selected seller and seller options (AdornSeller.json), edited player dialogue (AdornSellerDialogue.json), riddles, recipes, per-NPC author drafts, recording takes, and the BodySlide output-folder choice (settings.json). Review author content before distributing a Configs mod; personal legacy outfit files are not needed for a fresh player. Do not copy user data into either runtime mod."},{"title":"Saves, config & backups","group":"Reference","section":"Personal save data","path":"reference/user-data.html#personal-save-data","text":"## Personal save data Personal saved outfits, seller introduction/unlock, discovery, orders, learned recipes and tiered offer/history journals belong to the loaded save's .skse companion. New games start empty and locked while keeping shared author setup. Loading an earlier save restores its earlier personal state. Back up the matching game save and co-save together. Save after personal changes or an encounter reset. Old player-outfits.json files remain read-only recovery sources: Assign → Player → Saved outfits → Recover old saved outfits… copies them after confirmation. MCM → Adorn → Troubleshooting → Reset seller encounter… resets introduction/discovery and cancels a pending order, preserving outfits, learned recipes, completed rewards and fixed tiered offers."},{"title":"Saves, config & backups","group":"Reference","section":"Shared configuration and prepared output","path":"reference/user-data.html#shared-configuration-and-prepared-output","text":"## Shared configuration and prepared output The Adorn mod contains clean defaults and read-only stock voice catalogs. The clean Configs mod begins with editable copies of the starter seller, dialogue, riddles, and recipes plus empty assignment and draft files. An older empty player-outfit file may still be present; it is no longer the live wardrobe. Editable author JSON in the user-data folder takes precedence over shipped defaults and author saves go there. Personal progress is saved with the game. Custom dialogue provider and voice-job manifests still belong under SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/ in the authored output mod. The same destination also holds MCM/Settings/AdornSlots.ini, both generated SKSE/Plugins/SkyPatcher/{npc,outfit}/zzzzAdorn/zzAdornRules.ini files, and prepared ASF output (Adorn Seller Framework.esp, matching SEQ and Sound/Voice files). Check the actual MCM settings file in MO2 when backing up your bindings. These paths are imposed by MCM Helper, SkyPatcher, and Skyrim. The game save carries order progress and other save-bound state. The ASF publisher keeps its temporary build stage and extracted stock-audio cache under Windows Local AppData, outside the shareable data. The ASF runtime mod contains the framework ESP, scripts, FFmpeg, portable eSpeak and author tools. Its clean generic distribution contains no selected NPC, personal recordings or NPC-specific provider. Authored INFO and FUZ output needs Build, post-exit installation and restart. In-game playback must then be checked. OpenRouter's API key and model/persona/provider preferences are separate Windows Credential Manager entries for the same Windows account/PC. Neither belongs to these folders, game saves or exports. Use Assistance → Remove key to delete the key explicitly. Review the riddle maker manual before using optional assistance."},{"title":"Saves, config & backups","group":"Reference","section":"Share selected assignments","path":"reference/user-data.html#share-selected-assignments","text":"## Share selected assignments For selected NPC/faction contributions instead of sharing the whole configuration, use Assignments → Share assignments. Packs carry installed/custom looks, mixed recipient groups, enabled state, and faction exclusions; the recipient reviews conflicts before merging. See ASSIGNMENT_SHARING.md for paths, limits, and the local child-approval rule. Export pack opens Save As so you choose the output location. Import pack opens a file chooser and reviews a JSON directly from Downloads, Desktop, or another folder while Skyrim is running. Copying into Adorn Configs and restarting are not required to select/import a file. The AssignmentPacks folder is an optional modlist-supplied library, available under Installed packs (optional). Imported assignments become part of rules.json. Removing their source pack does not remove accepted assignments. Test in a separate configuration: another save or MO2 profile can still use the same Adorn Configs directory. Review the accepted rules and their exclusions; restart Skyrim to apply the generated next-launch rules."},{"title":"Saves, config & backups","group":"Reference","section":"Reset with Adorn Configs","path":"reference/user-data.html#reset-with-adorn-configs","text":"## Reset with Adorn Configs For a character's seller encounter, use the MCM recovery action instead of changing installation files. Confirming Reset cancels a pending order and clears introduction/discovery for the current save, preserving completed rewards and fixed tiered offers. The next first order says Find seller until you speak to them; pending answers remain hidden even for authors. New games do not require manual reset. For a clean author configuration, first back up and identify all Adorn-generated files in Configs and Overwrite, including SkyPatcher INIs, MCM settings, JSON and matching ASF ESP/SEQ/voices. Isolate that known set in a separate configuration; do not delete or clear Overwrite. Existing Overwrite files can otherwise override the starter. Disabling Configs alone does not remove those overrides or personal save progress. Clean shipped seller JSON is disabled with no NPC. Developer tools unlocked shows local author state after acceptance; unticking clears the credential. A blank input alone does not mean locked. This resets installation-level author data. An existing Skyrim save still contains its own order history, learned recipes, quest state, and any actor changes already saved by the game. Use a new save for a completely blank gameplay state. Share Adorn Configs as a third MO2 mod below Adorn and ASF in MO2's left pane; do not include unrelated Overwrite files or the Local AppData build cache."},{"title":"ASF files & formats","group":"Reference","section":"","path":"reference/files.html","text":"ASF’s prepared conversation is a set of matching records, manifests, sequence data and voice files. Use this reference when inspecting build output or packaging a seller, so the files describing one build stay together and their format versions are understood."},{"title":"ASF files & formats","group":"Reference","section":"Files and provider output","path":"reference/files.html#files-and-provider-output","text":"## Files and provider output Paths below are Data-relative under the resolved user-data root. | File/directory | Responsibility | | --- | --- | | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/AdornSeller.json | Placed seller and options | | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/AdornSellerAuthorDrafts.json | Conversations per NPC base | | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/AdornSellerDialogue.json | Generic/start template and migration input | | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/AdornRiddles.json | Riddles/profiles/rules | | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/AdornRecipes.json | Recipe templates | | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/AdornSellerAuthorRecordings | Sources, selections, trims and bindings | | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/publish-job.json and publish-status.json | Build request/result | | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/AdornSellerProviders.json | Installed NPC routing | | SKSE/Plugins/Adorn/AdornSellerVoiceJobs.json | Exact INFO/reply/audio jobs | | Adorn Seller Framework.esp and matching SEQ | Prepared dialogue records/sequence | | Sound/Voice/Adorn Seller Framework.esp/VoiceType/.fuz | Final playable voice/lip files | | Windows Local AppData seller-build folder | Logs, temporary stages and extracted stock cache | | Game save and matching .skse | Personal looks/progress, recipes and offer journal | FUZ filenames derive from INFO records, not take names or runtime IDs. Preserve the matching plugin, SEQ, manifests and voice tree. The provider format remains version 2 with additive clue metadata; author riddle/recipe documents remain version 1. Progress serialization is version 6. These are format versions, not public mod versions. ### Advanced providers and compatibility Automatic Build is the normal route. An author placing seller INFOs in an NPC mod/patch must preserve ASF conditions/actions and exact voice paths. Required INFO existence is not proof of correct conditions, fragments, audio or winning files. Use Open build logs in the seller dialogue editor to inspect build diagnostics. Preserve ordinary follower/quest dialogue. If an older mod already adds Adorn-specific opening/hand-in choices, adapt or disable the obsolete duplicate in a compatibility patch."},{"title":"Artwork & credits","group":"Reference","section":"","path":"reference/credits.html","text":"This page identifies the branding and typography used by the Adorn and Adorn Seller Framework (ASF) wiki. It also explains where the guides come from and preserves the supplied font’s usage notice."},{"title":"Artwork & credits","group":"Reference","section":"Adorn branding","path":"reference/credits.html#adorn-branding","text":"## Adorn branding This wiki uses the supplied Adorn wordmark v4, copied from the release artwork. The original PNG remains unchanged."},{"title":"Artwork & credits","group":"Reference","section":"Typography","path":"reference/credits.html#typography","text":"## Typography Headings, navigation and controls use the same Dumbledor typeface supplied with Adorn. The font is credited to Graham Meade / GemFonts. Its accompanying usage notice is included with the copied font. Long-form body copy uses your device's system fonts for comfortable reading. The four colour themes use Adorn's interface palette with opaque backgrounds suited to reading outside the game."},{"title":"Artwork & credits","group":"Reference","section":"Documentation","path":"reference/credits.html#documentation","text":"## Documentation The guides are generated from the maintained Adorn and ASF documentation. Player instructions, author tools and technical reference have separate navigation, and release/testing boundaries remain visible."}];
